---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucket
---@field customResponseHeaders? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Headers that the Application Load Balancer should add to proxied responses.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field loadBalancingScheme? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketLoadBalancingSchemeEnum The value can only be INTERNAL_MANAGED for cross-region internal layer 7 load balancer. If loadBalancingScheme is not specified, the backend bucket can be used by classic global external load balancers, or global application external load balancers, or both.
