---The configuration for a custom policy implemented by the user and
---deployed with the client.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfigCustomPolicy
---@field data? string An optional, arbitrary JSON object with configuration data, understood by a locally installed custom policy implementation.
---@field name? string Identifies the custom policy. The value should match the name of a custom implementation registered on the gRPC clients. It should follow protocol buffer message naming conventions and include the full path (for example, myorg.CustomLbPolicy). The maximum length is 256 characters. Do not specify the same custom policy more than once for a backend. If you do, the configuration is rejected. For an example of how to use this field, seeUse a custom policy.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfig[]

---The configuration for a built-in load balancing policy.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfigPolicy
---@field name? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfigPolicyNameEnum|string The name of a locality load-balancing policy. Valid values include ROUND_ROBIN and, for Java clients, LEAST_REQUEST. For information about these values, see the description of localityLbPolicy. Do not specify the same policy more than once for a backend. If you do, the configuration is rejected.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLocalityLoadBalancingPolicyConfigPolicyNameEnum "INVALID_LB_POLICY"|"LEAST_REQUEST"|"MAGLEV"|"ORIGINAL_DESTINATION"|"RANDOM"|"RING_HASH"|"ROUND_ROBIN"|"WEIGHTED_GCP_RENDEZVOUS"|"WEIGHTED_MAGLEV"|"WEIGHTED_ROUND_ROBIN"

---The available logging options for the load balancer traffic served by this
---backend service.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfig
---@field enable? boolean Denotes whether to enable logging for the load balancer traffic served by this backend service. The default value is false.
---@field optionalFields? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList This field can only be specified if logging is enabled for this backend service and "logConfig.optionalMode" was set to CUSTOM. Contains a list of optional fields you want to include in the logs. For example: serverInstance, serverGkeDetails.cluster, serverGkeDetails.pod.podNamespace
---@field loggingHttpResponseHeaders? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigLoggingHttpHeaderList The list of response headers that will be logged to Stackdriver.
---@field sampleRate? number This field can only be specified if logging is enabled for this backend service. The value of the field must be in [0, 1]. This configures the sampling rate of requests to the load balancer where 1.0 means all logged requests are reported and 0.0 means no logged requests are reported. The default value is 1.0.
---@field optionalMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigOptionalModeEnum|string This field can only be specified if logging is enabled for this backend service. Configures whether all, none or a subset of optional fields should be added to the reported logs. One of [INCLUDE_ALL_OPTIONAL, EXCLUDE_ALL_OPTIONAL, CUSTOM]. Default is EXCLUDE_ALL_OPTIONAL.
---@field loggingHttpRequestHeaders? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigLoggingHttpHeaderList The list of request headers that will be logged to Stackdriver.

---Determines which HTTP headers will be logged to Stackdriver.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigLoggingHttpHeader
---@field headerName? string The name of the header to be logged.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigLoggingHttpHeaderList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigLoggingHttpHeader[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceLogConfigOptionalModeEnum "CUSTOM"|"EXCLUDE_ALL_OPTIONAL"|"INCLUDE_ALL_OPTIONAL"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceNetworkPassThroughLbTrafficPolicy
---@field zonalAffinity? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceNetworkPassThroughLbTrafficPolicyZonalAffinity When configured, new connections are load balanced across healthy backend endpoints in the local zone.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceNetworkPassThroughLbTrafficPolicyZonalAffinity
---@field spillover? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceNetworkPassThroughLbTrafficPolicyZonalAffinitySpilloverEnum|string This field indicates whether zonal affinity is enabled or not. The possible values are: - ZONAL_AFFINITY_DISABLED: Default Value. Zonal Affinity is disabled. The load balancer distributes new connections to all healthy backend endpoints across all zones. - ZONAL_AFFINITY_STAY_WITHIN_ZONE: Zonal Affinity is enabled. The load balancer distributes new connections to all healthy backend endpoints in the local zone only. If there are no healthy backend endpoints in the local zone, the load balancer distributes new connections to all backend endpoints in the local zone. - ZONAL_AFFINITY_SPILL_CROSS_ZONE: Zonal Affinity is enabled. The load balancer distributes new connections to all healthy backend endpoints in the local zone only. If there aren't enough healthy backend endpoints in the local zone, the load balancer distributes new connections to all healthy backend endpoints across all zones.
---@field spilloverRatio? number The value of the field must be in [0, 1]. When the ratio of the count of healthy backend endpoints in a zone to the count of backend endpoints in that same zone is equal to or above this threshold, the load balancer distributes new connections to all healthy endpoints in the local zone only. When the ratio of the count of healthy backend endpoints in a zone to the count of backend endpoints in that same zone is below this threshold, the load balancer distributes all new connections to all healthy endpoints across all zones.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendServiceNetworkPassThroughLbTrafficPolicyZonalAffinitySpilloverEnum "ZONAL_AFFINITY_DISABLED"|"ZONAL_AFFINITY_SPILL_CROSS_ZONE"|"ZONAL_AFFINITY_STAY_WITHIN_ZONE"

