---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyPolicySourceEnum "SYSTEM"|"USER_DEFINED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyPolicyTypeEnum "RDMA_FALCON_POLICY"|"RDMA_ROCE_POLICY"|"ULL_POLICY"|"VPC_POLICY"

---Represents a rule that describes one or more match conditions along with
---the action to be taken when traffic matches this condition (allow or deny).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRule
---@field direction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleDirectionEnum|string The direction in which this rule applies.
---@field targetSecureTags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleSecureTagList A list of secure tags that controls which instances the firewall rule applies to. If targetSecureTag are specified, then the firewall rule applies only to instances in the VPC network that have one of those EFFECTIVE secure tags, if all the target_secure_tag are in INEFFECTIVE state, then this rule will be ignored.targetSecureTag may not be set at the same time astargetServiceAccounts. If neither targetServiceAccounts nortargetSecureTag are specified, the firewall rule applies to all instances on the specified network. Maximum number of target label tags allowed is 256.
---@field ruleTupleCount? number Output only. [Output Only] Calculation of the complexity of a single firewall policy rule.
---@field targetResources? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of network resource URLs to which this rule applies. This field allows you to control which network's VMs get this rule. If this field is left blank, all VMs within the organization will receive the rule.
---@field targetServiceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of service accounts indicating the sets of instances that are applied with this rule.
---@field targetForwardingRules? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of forwarding rules to which this rule applies. This field allows you to control which load balancers get this rule. For example, the following are valid values: - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/global/forwardingRules/forwardingRule - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/regions/region/forwardingRules/forwardingRule - projects/project/global/ forwardingRules/forwardingRule - projects/project/regions/region/forwardingRules/ forwardingRule
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output only] Type of the resource. Returnscompute#firewallPolicyRule for firewall rules andcompute#packetMirroringRule for packet mirroring rules.
---@field priority? number An integer indicating the priority of a rule in the list. The priority must be a positive value between 0 and 2147483647. Rules are evaluated from highest to lowest priority where 0 is the highest priority and 2147483647 is the lowest priority.
---@field disabled? boolean Denotes whether the firewall policy rule is disabled. When set to true, the firewall policy rule is not enforced and traffic behaves as if it did not exist. If this is unspecified, the firewall policy rule will be enabled.
---@field action? string The Action to perform when the client connection triggers the rule. Valid actions for firewall rules are: "allow", "deny", "apply_security_profile_group" and "goto_next" ( "apply_security_profile_group" can be specified only for global network firewall policies or hierarchical firewall policies). Valid actions for packet mirroring rules are: "mirror", "do_not_mirror" and "goto_next".
---@field ruleName? string An optional name for the rule. This field is not a unique identifier and can be updated.
---@field targetType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleTargetTypeEnum|string Target types of the firewall policy rule. Default value is INSTANCES.
---@field description? string An optional description for this resource.
---@field match? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcher A match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against. If it evaluates to true, the corresponding 'action' is enforced.
---@field securityProfileGroup? string A fully-qualified URL of a SecurityProfileGroup resource instance. Example: https://networksecurity.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{project}/locations/{location}/securityProfileGroups/my-security-profile-group Must be specified if action is one of 'apply_security_profile_group' or 'mirror'. Cannot be specified for other actions. Can be specified only for global network firewall policies or hierarchical firewall policies.
---@field enableLogging? boolean Denotes whether to enable logging for a particular rule. If logging is enabled, logs will be exported to the configured export destination in Stackdriver. Logs may be exported to BigQuery or Pub/Sub. Note: you cannot enable logging on "goto_next" rules.
---@field tlsInspect? boolean Boolean flag indicating if the traffic should be TLS decrypted. Can be set only if action = 'apply_security_profile_group' and cannot be set for other actions.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleDirectionEnum "EGRESS"|"INGRESS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRule[]

---Represents a match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against.
---Exactly one field must be specified.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcher
---@field srcNetworkType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherSrcNetworkTypeEnum|string Network type of the traffic source. Allowed values are: - UNSPECIFIED - INTERNET - INTRA_VPC - NON_INTERNET - VPC_NETWORKS
---@field destNetworkContext? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherDestNetworkContextEnum|string Network context of the traffic destination. Allowed values are: - UNSPECIFIED - INTERNET - NON_INTERNET
---@field destAddressGroups? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Address groups which should be matched against the traffic destination. Maximum number of destination address groups is 10.
---@field destNetworkScope? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherDestNetworkScopeEnum|string Network scope of the traffic destination.
---@field srcAddressGroups? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Address groups which should be matched against the traffic source. Maximum number of source address groups is 10.
---@field destNetworkType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherDestNetworkTypeEnum|string Network type of the traffic destination. Allowed values are: - UNSPECIFIED - INTERNET - NON_INTERNET
---@field layer4Configs? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherLayer4ConfigList Pairs of IP protocols and ports that the rule should match.
---@field srcNetworkContext? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherSrcNetworkContextEnum|string Network context of the traffic source. Allowed values are: - UNSPECIFIED - INTERNET - INTRA_VPC - NON_INTERNET - VPC_NETWORKS
---@field srcNetworkScope? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleMatcherSrcNetworkScopeEnum|string Network scope of the traffic source.
---@field destThreatIntelligences? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Names of Network Threat Intelligence lists. The IPs in these lists will be matched against traffic destination.
---@field destRegionCodes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Region codes whose IP addresses will be used to match for destination of traffic. Should be specified as 2 letter country code defined as per ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes. ex."US" Maximum number of dest region codes allowed is 5000.
---@field destIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of destination CIDR IP ranges allowed is 5000.
---@field srcNetworks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Networks of the traffic source. It can be either a full or partial url.
---@field srcThreatIntelligences? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Names of Network Threat Intelligence lists. The IPs in these lists will be matched against traffic source.
---@field srcRegionCodes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Region codes whose IP addresses will be used to match for source of traffic. Should be specified as 2 letter country code defined as per ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes. ex."US" Maximum number of source region codes allowed is 5000.
---@field srcFqdns? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) which should be matched against traffic source. Maximum number of source fqdn allowed is 100.
---@field srcSecureTags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FirewallPolicyRuleSecureTagList List of secure tag values, which should be matched at the source of the traffic. For INGRESS rule, if all the srcSecureTag are INEFFECTIVE, and there is no srcIpRange, this rule will be ignored. Maximum number of source tag values allowed is 256.
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of source CIDR IP ranges allowed is 5000.
---@field destFqdns? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) which should be matched against traffic destination. Maximum number of destination fqdn allowed is 100.

