---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservation
---@field protectionTier? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationProtectionTierEnum Protection tier for the workload.
---@field aggregateReservation? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AllocationAggregateReservation Aggregate reservation details for the future reservation.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field shareSettings? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShareSettings List of Projects/Folders to share with.
---@field commitmentInfo? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationCommitmentInfo If not present, then FR will not deliver a new commitment or update an existing commitment.
---@field timeWindow? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationTimeWindow Time window for this Future Reservation.
---@field storagePoolProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationStoragePoolProperties Storage pool details for the future reservation.
---@field schedulingType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationSchedulingTypeEnum Maintenance information for this reservation
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the future reservation.
---@field confidentialComputeType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationConfidentialComputeTypeEnum
---@field planningStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationPlanningStatusEnum Planning state before being submitted for evaluation
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] A unique identifier for this future reservation. The server defines this identifier.
---@field deploymentType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationDeploymentTypeEnum Type of the deployment requested as part of future reservation.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#futureReservation for future reservations.
---@field specificReservationRequired? boolean Indicates whether the auto-created reservation can be consumed by VMs with affinity for "any" reservation. If the field is set, then only VMs that target the reservation by name can consume from the delivered reservation.
---@field reservationMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationReservationModeEnum The reservation mode which determines reservation-termination behavior and expected pricing.
---@field reservationName? string Name of reservations where the capacity is provisioned at the time of delivery of future reservations. If the reservation with the given name does not exist already, it is created automatically at the time of Approval with INACTIVE state till specified start-time. Either provide the reservation_name or a name_prefix.
---@field advancedDeploymentControl? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControl Advanced control for cluster management, applicable only to DENSE deployment type future reservations.
---@field enableEmergentMaintenance? boolean Indicates if this group of VMs have emergent maintenance enabled.
---@field colocationResource? string Full or partial URL of an existing future reservation to indicate intent for reserving capacity in the same cluster as the colocation resource.
---@field autoDeleteAutoCreatedReservations? boolean Setting for enabling or disabling automatic deletion for auto-created reservation. If set to true, auto-created reservations will be deleted at Future Reservation's end time (default) or at user's defined timestamp if any of the [auto_created_reservations_delete_time, auto_created_reservations_duration] values is specified. For keeping auto-created reservation indefinitely, this value should be set to false.
---@field autoCreatedReservationsDeleteTime? string Future timestamp when the FR auto-created reservations will be deleted by Compute Engine. Format of this field must be a valid href="https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt">RFC3339 value.
---@field autoCreatedReservationsDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Specifies the duration of auto-created reservations. It represents relative time to future reservation start_time when auto-created reservations will be automatically deleted by Compute Engine. Duration time unit is represented as a count of seconds and fractions of seconds at nanosecond resolution.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationParams Input only. Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] The creation timestamp for this future reservation inRFC3339 text format.
---@field namePrefix? string Name prefix for the reservations to be created at the time of delivery. The name prefix must comply with RFC1035. Maximum allowed length for name prefix is 20. Automatically created reservations name format will be -date-####.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationStatus Output only. [Output only] Status of the Future Reservation
---@field zone? string Output only. [Output Only] URL of the Zone where this future reservation resides.
---@field specificSkuProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationSpecificSKUProperties Future Reservation configuration to indicate instance properties and total count.
---@field resourceName? string Name of the resource intended to be delivered. Name should conform to RFC1035. This will be the name of storage pool or Exapool for persistent disk FRs.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined fully-qualified URL for this resource.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationCommitmentInfo
---@field commitmentPlan? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationCommitmentInfoCommitmentPlanEnum|string Indicates if a Commitment needs to be created as part of FR delivery. If this field is not present, then no commitment needs to be created.
---@field previousCommitmentTerms? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FutureReservationCommitmentInfoPreviousCommitmentTermsEnum|string Only applicable if FR is delivering to the same reservation. If set, all parent commitments will be extended to match the end date of the plan for this commitment.
---@field commitmentName? string name of the commitment where capacity is being delivered to.

