---@field confidentialInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ConfidentialInstanceConfig
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Resource policies applied to this instance.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource.
---@field lastStartTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last start timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field resourceStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ResourceStatus Output only. [Output Only] Specifies values set for instance attributes as compared to the values requested by user in the corresponding input only field.
---@field machineType? string Full or partial URL of the machine type resource to use for this instance, in the format:zones/zone/machineTypes/machine-type. This is provided by the client when the instance is created. For example, the following is a valid partial url to a predefined machine type: zones/us-central1-f/machineTypes/n1-standard-1 To create acustom machine type, provide a URL to a machine type in the following format, where CPUS is 1 or an even number up to 32 (2, 4, 6, ... 24, etc), and MEMORY is the total memory for this instance. Memory must be a multiple of 256 MB and must be supplied in MB (e.g. 5 GB of memory is 5120 MB): zones/zone/machineTypes/custom-CPUS-MEMORY For example: zones/us-central1-f/machineTypes/custom-4-5120 For a full list of restrictions, read theSpecifications for custom machine types.
---@field networkInterfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.NetworkInterfaceList An array of network configurations for this instance. These specify how interfaces are configured to interact with other network services, such as connecting to the internet. Multiple interfaces are supported per instance.
---@field lastSuspendedTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last suspended timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field deletionProtection? boolean Whether the resource should be protected against deletion.
---@field localSsdEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum|string Specifies which method should be used for encrypting the Local SSDs attached to the VM.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field shieldedVmIntegrityPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShieldedVmIntegrityPolicy Output only. Deprecating, please use shielded_instance_integrity_policy.
---@field canIpForward? boolean Allows this instance to send and receive packets with non-matching destination or source IPs. This is required if you plan to use this instance to forward routes. For more information, seeEnabling IP Forwarding.
---@field cpuPlatform? string Output only. [Output Only] The CPU platform used by this instance.
---@field lastStopTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last stop timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Metadata The metadata key/value pairs assigned to this instance. This includes metadata keys that were explicitly defined for the instance.
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. [Output Only] An optional, human-readable explanation of the status.
---@field postKeyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum|string PostKeyRevocationActionType of the instance.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field sourceMachineImage? string Specifies the machine image to use to create the instance. This field is optional. It can be a full or partial URL. For example, the following are all valid URLs to a machine image: - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/global/global/machineImages/machineImage - projects/project/global/global/machineImages/machineImage - global/machineImages/machineImage
---@field zone string The name of the zone for this request.
---@field sourceInstanceTemplate? string Specifies instance template to create the instance. This field is optional. It can be a full or partial URL. For example, the following are all valid URLs to an instance template: - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate - projects/project/global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate - global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

