---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerAllInstancesConfig
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesPatch Properties to set on all instances in the group. You can add or modify properties using theinstanceGroupManagers.patch orregionInstanceGroupManagers.patch. After settingallInstancesConfig on the group, you must update the group's instances to apply the configuration. To apply the configuration, set the group's updatePolicy.type field to use proactive updates or use the applyUpdatesToInstances method.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerAutoHealingPolicy
---@field healthCheck? string The URL for the health check that signals autohealing.
---@field initialDelaySec? number The initial delay is the number of seconds that a new VM takes to initialize and run its startup script. During a VM's initial delay period, the MIG ignores unsuccessful health checks because the VM might be in the startup process. This prevents the MIG from prematurely recreating a VM. If the health check receives a healthy response during the initial delay, it indicates that the startup process is complete and the VM is ready. The value of initial delay must be between 0 and 3600 seconds. The default value is 0.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerAutoHealingPolicyList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerAutoHealingPolicy[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerFailoverActionEnum "NO_FAILOVER"|"UNKNOWN"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicy
---@field provisioningModelMix? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyProvisioningModelMix Provisioning model configuration used by this managed instance group to create instances.
---@field instanceSelections? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyInstanceSelectionMap Named instance selections configuring properties that the group will use when creating new VMs.
---@field constraints? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyConstraints Constraints applied to instance flexibility spreading and selection.

---Constraints applied to instance flexibility spreading and selection.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyConstraints
---@field singleMachineType? boolean When set to true, all instances in the group will be provisioned with the exact same machine type, ensuring cluster homogeneity across zones. Defaults to false.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyInstanceSelection
---@field machineTypes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Full machine-type names, e.g. "n1-standard-16".
---@field rank? number Preference of this instance selection. Lower number means higher preference. MIG will first try to create a VM based on the machine-type with lowest rank and fallback to next rank based on availability. Machine types and instance selections with the same rank have the same preference.
---@field minCpuPlatform? string Name of the minimum CPU platform to be used by this instance selection. e.g. 'Intel Ice Lake'.
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AttachedDiskList List of disks to be attached to the instances created from this selection.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyInstanceSelectionMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyInstanceSelection }

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceFlexibilityPolicyProvisioningModelMix
---@field standardCapacityBase? number The base capacity that will always use Standard VMs to avoid risk of more preemption than the minimum capacity user needs. MIG will create only Standard VMs until it reaches standard_capacity_base and only then will start using standard_capacity_percent_above_base to mix Spot with Standard VMs.
---@field standardCapacityPercentAboveBase? number The percentage of target capacity that should use Standard VM. The remaining percentage will use Spot VMs. The percentage applies only to the capacity above standard_capacity_base.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicy
---@field onRepair? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnRepair Configuration for VM repairs in the MIG.
---@field defaultActionOnFailure? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyDefaultActionOnFailureEnum|string The action that a MIG performs on a failed VM. If the value of the onFailedHealthCheck field is `DEFAULT_ACTION`, then the same action also applies to the VMs on which your application fails a health check. Valid values are - REPAIR (default): MIG automatically repairs a failed VM by recreating it. For more information, see About repairing VMs in a MIG. - DO_NOTHING: MIG does not repair a failed VM.
---@field onFailedHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnFailedHealthCheckEnum|string The action that a MIG performs on an unhealthy VM. A VM is marked as unhealthy when the application running on that VM fails a health check. Valid values are: - DEFAULT_ACTION (default): MIG uses the same action configured for instanceLifecyclePolicy.defaultActionOnFailure field. - REPAIR: MIG automatically repairs an unhealthy VM by recreating it. - DO_NOTHING: MIG doesn't repair an unhealthy VM. For more information, see About repairing VMs in a MIG.
---@field forceUpdateOnRepair? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyForceUpdateOnRepairEnum|string A bit indicating whether to forcefully apply the group's latest configuration when repairing a VM. Valid options are: - NO (default): If configuration updates are available, they are not forcefully applied during repair. Instead, configuration updates are applied according to the group's update policy. - YES: If configuration updates are available, they are applied during repair.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyDefaultActionOnFailureEnum "DELETE"|"DO_NOTHING"|"REPAIR"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyForceUpdateOnRepairEnum "NO"|"YES"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnFailedHealthCheckEnum "DEFAULT_ACTION"|"DO_NOTHING"|"REPAIR"

---Configuration for VM repairs in the MIG.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnRepair
---@field allowChangingZone? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnRepairAllowChangingZoneEnum|string Specifies whether the MIG can change a VM's zone during a repair. Valid values are: - NO (default): MIG cannot change a VM's zone during a repair. - YES: MIG can select a different zone for the VM during a repair.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerInstanceLifecyclePolicyOnRepairAllowChangingZoneEnum "NO"|"YES"

