---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerStandbyPolicy
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerStandbyPolicyModeEnum|string Defines how a MIG resumes or starts VMs from a standby pool when the group scales out. The default mode is `MANUAL`.
---@field initialDelaySec? number Specifies the number of seconds that the MIG should wait to suspend or stop a VM after that VM was created. The initial delay gives the initialization script the time to prepare your VM for a quick scale out. The value of initial delay must be between 0 and 3600 seconds. The default value is 0.

