---@field nonExistent? number Output only. The number of instances that have not been created yet or have been deleted. Includes only instances that would be shown in the listManagedInstances method and not all instances that have been deleted in the lifetime of the MIG. Does not include FlexStart instances that are waiting for the resources availability, they are considered as 'pending'.
---@field deprovisioning? number Output only. The number of instances in the managed instance group that have DEPROVISIONING status.
---@field stopped? number Output only. The number of instances in the managed instance group that have STOPPED status.
---@field repairing? number Output only. The number of instances in the managed instance group that have REPAIRING status.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerStatusStateful
---@field perInstanceConfigs? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerStatusStatefulPerInstanceConfigs Output only. Status of per-instance configurations on the instances.
---@field hasStatefulConfig? boolean Output only. A bit indicating whether the managed instance group has stateful configuration, that is, if you have configured any items in a stateful policy or in per-instance configs. The group might report that it has no stateful configuration even when there is still some preserved state on a managed instance, for example, if you have deleted all PICs but not yet applied those deletions.
---@field isStateful? boolean Output only. A bit indicating whether the managed instance group has stateful configuration, that is, if you have configured any items in a stateful policy or in per-instance configs. The group might report that it has no stateful configuration even when there is still some preserved state on a managed instance, for example, if you have deleted all PICs but not yet applied those deletions. This field is deprecated in favor of has_stateful_config.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerStatusStatefulPerInstanceConfigs
