---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerTargetSizePolicy
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerTargetSizePolicyModeEnum|string The mode of target size policy based on which the MIG creates its VMs individually or all at once.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerTargetSizePolicyModeEnum "BULK"|"INDIVIDUAL"|"UNSPECIFIED_MODE"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicy
---@field minimalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyMinimalActionEnum|string Minimal action to be taken on an instance. Use this option to minimize disruption as much as possible or to apply a more disruptive action than is necessary. - To limit disruption as much as possible, set the minimal action toREFRESH. If your update requires a more disruptive action, Compute Engine performs the necessary action to execute the update. - To apply a more disruptive action than is strictly necessary, set the minimal action to RESTART or REPLACE. For example, Compute Engine does not need to restart a VM to change its metadata. But if your application reads instance metadata only when a VM is restarted, you can set the minimal action to RESTART in order to pick up metadata changes.
---@field instanceRedistributionType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyInstanceRedistributionTypeEnum|string The instance redistribution policy for regional managed instance groups. Valid values are: - PROACTIVE (default): The group attempts to maintain an even distribution of VM instances across zones in the region. - NONE: For non-autoscaled groups, proactive redistribution is disabled.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyTypeEnum|string The type of update process. You can specify either PROACTIVE so that the MIG automatically updates VMs to the latest configurations orOPPORTUNISTIC so that you can select the VMs that you want to update.
---@field maxUnavailable? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FixedOrPercent The maximum number of instances that can be unavailable during the update process. An instance is considered available if all of the following conditions are satisfied: - The instance's status is RUNNING. - If there is a health check on the instance group, the instance's health check status must be HEALTHY at least once. If there is no health check on the group, then the instance only needs to have a status of RUNNING to be considered available. This value can be either a fixed number or, if the group has 10 or more instances, a percentage. If you set a percentage, the number of instances is rounded if necessary. The default value formaxUnavailable is a fixed value equal to the number of zones in which the managed instance group operates. At least one of either maxSurge ormaxUnavailable must be greater than 0. Learn more about maxUnavailable.
---@field replacementMethod? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyReplacementMethodEnum|string What action should be used to replace instances. See minimal_action.REPLACE
---@field minReadySec? number Minimum number of seconds to wait for after a newly created instance becomes available. This value must be from range [0, 3600].
---@field mostDisruptiveAllowedAction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyMostDisruptiveAllowedActionEnum|string Most disruptive action that is allowed to be taken on an instance. You can specify either NONE to forbid any actions,REFRESH to avoid restarting the VM and to limit disruption as much as possible. RESTART to allow actions that can be applied without instance replacing or REPLACE to allow all possible actions. If the Updater determines that the minimal update action needed is more disruptive than most disruptive allowed action you specify it will not perform the update at all.
---@field allowedActions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyAllowedActionsItemEnumList Actions that are allowed to update instances within MIG.
---@field maxSurge? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.FixedOrPercent The maximum number of instances that can be created above the specifiedtargetSize during the update process. This value can be either a fixed number or, if the group has 10 or more instances, a percentage. If you set a percentage, the number of instances is rounded if necessary. The default value for maxSurge is a fixed value equal to the number of zones in which the managed instance group operates. At least one of either maxSurge ormaxUnavailable must be greater than 0. Learn more about maxSurge.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyAllowedActionsItemEnum "NONE"|"REFRESH"|"REPLACE"|"RESTART"|"RESTART_IN_PLACE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyAllowedActionsItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyAllowedActionsItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyInstanceRedistributionTypeEnum "NONE"|"PROACTIVE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyMinimalActionEnum "NONE"|"REFRESH"|"REPLACE"|"RESTART"|"RESTART_IN_PLACE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyMostDisruptiveAllowedActionEnum "NONE"|"REFRESH"|"REPLACE"|"RESTART"|"RESTART_IN_PLACE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceGroupManagerUpdatePolicyReplacementMethodEnum "RECREATE"|"SUBSTITUTE"

