---Additional instance params.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceParams
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Input only. Resource manager tags to be bound to the instance. Tag keys and values have the same definition as resource manager tags. Keys and values can be either in numeric format, such as `tagKeys/{tag_key_id}` and `tagValues/{tag_value_id}` or in namespaced format such as `{org_id|project_id}/{tag_key_short_name}` and `{tag_value_short_name}`. The field is ignored (both PUT & PATCH) when empty.
---@field requestValidForDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Relative deadline for waiting for capacity. Relevant only for Instances.Insert API.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum "NOOP"|"POST_KEY_REVOCATION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SHUTDOWN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum "ENABLE_BIDIRECTIONAL_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"ENABLE_OUTBOUND_VM_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceProperties
---@field advancedMachineFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AdvancedMachineFeatures Controls for advanced machine-related behavior features. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field guestAccelerators? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AcceleratorConfigList A list of guest accelerator cards' type and count to use for instances created from these properties.
---@field minCpuPlatform? string Minimum cpu/platform to be used by instances. The instance may be scheduled on the specified or newer cpu/platform. Applicable values are the friendly names of CPU platforms, such asminCpuPlatform: "Intel Haswell" orminCpuPlatform: "Intel Sandy Bridge". For more information, read Specifying a Minimum CPU Platform.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationAffinity Specifies the reservations that instances can consume from. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field canIpForward? boolean Enables instances created based on these properties to send packets with source IP addresses other than their own and receive packets with destination IP addresses other than their own. If these instances will be used as an IP gateway or it will be set as the next-hop in a Route resource, specify true. If unsure, leave this set tofalse. See theEnable IP forwarding documentation for more information.
---@field networkPerformanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.NetworkPerformanceConfig Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Input only. Resource manager tags to be bound to the instance. Tag keys and values have the same definition as resource manager tags. Keys and values can be either in numeric format, such as `tagKeys/{tag_key_id}` and `tagValues/{tag_value_id}` or in namespaced format such as `{org_id|project_id}/{tag_key_short_name}` and `{tag_value_short_name}`. The field is ignored (both PUT & PATCH) when empty.
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Tags A list of tags to apply to the instances that are created from these properties. The tags identify valid sources or targets for network firewalls. The setTags method can modify this list of tags. Each tag within the list must comply with RFC1035.
---@field privateIpv6GoogleAccess? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesPrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum|string The private IPv6 google access type for VMs. If not specified, use INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK as default. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field serviceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ServiceAccountList A list of service accounts with specified scopes. Access tokens for these service accounts are available to the instances that are created from these properties. Use metadata queries to obtain the access tokens for these instances.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShieldedVmConfig Specifies the Shielded VM options for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field confidentialInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ConfidentialInstanceConfig Specifies the Confidential Instance options. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field description? string An optional text description for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field shieldedInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShieldedInstanceConfig Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field displayDevice? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.DisplayDevice Display Device properties to enable support for remote display products like: Teradici, VNC and TeamViewer Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field scheduling? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Scheduling Specifies the scheduling options for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field networkInterfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.NetworkInterfaceList An array of network access configurations for this interface.
---@field keyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum|string KeyRevocationActionType of the instance. Supported options are "STOP" and "NONE". The default value is "NONE" if it is not specified.
---@field machineType? string The machine type to use for instances that are created from these properties. This field only accepts a machine type name, for example `n2-standard-4`. If you use the machine type full or partial URL, for example `projects/my-l7ilb-project/zones/us-central1-a/machineTypes/n2-standard-4`, the request will result in an `INTERNAL_ERROR`.
---@field localSsdEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum|string Specifies which method should be used for encrypting the Local SSDs attached to the VM.
---@field postKeyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesPostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum|string PostKeyRevocationActionType of the instance.
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Resource policies (names, not URLs) applied to instances created from these properties. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AttachedDiskList An array of disks that are associated with the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Labels to apply to instances that are created from these properties.
---@field partnerMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StructuredEntriesMap Partner Metadata assigned to the instance properties. A map from a subdomain (namespace) to entries map.
---@field workloadIdentityConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WorkloadIdentityConfig
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Metadata The metadata key/value pairs to assign to instances that are created from these properties. These pairs can consist of custom metadata or predefined keys. SeeProject and instance metadata for more information.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum "KEY_REVOCATION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"STOP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePropertiesLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum "CMEK_ENCRYPTION"|"EPHEMERAL_KEY_ENCRYPTION"|"LOCAL_SSD_ENCRYPTION_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD_ENCRYPTION"

