---Diagnostics information about the Interconnect connection, which contains
---detailed and current technical information about Google's side of the
---connection.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnostics
---@field links? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusList A list of InterconnectDiagnostics.LinkStatus objects, describing the status for each link on the Interconnect.
---@field bundleOperationalStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsBundleOperationalStatusEnum The operational status of the bundle interface.
---@field macAddress? string The MAC address of the Interconnect's bundle interface.
---@field bundleAggregationType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsBundleAggregationTypeEnum The aggregation type of the bundle interface.
---@field arpCaches? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntryList A list of InterconnectDiagnostics.ARPEntry objects, describing individual neighbors currently seen by the Google router in the ARP cache for the Interconnect. This will be empty when the Interconnect is not bundled.

---Describing the ARP neighbor entries seen on this link
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntry
---@field ipAddress? string The IP address of this ARP neighbor.
---@field macAddress? string The MAC address of this ARP neighbor.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntryList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntry[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsBundleAggregationTypeEnum "BUNDLE_AGGREGATION_TYPE_LACP"|"BUNDLE_AGGREGATION_TYPE_STATIC"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsBundleOperationalStatusEnum "BUNDLE_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_DOWN"|"BUNDLE_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_UP"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkLACPStatus
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkLACPStatusStateEnum The state of a LACP link, which can take one of the following values: - ACTIVE: The link is configured and active within the bundle. - DETACHED: The link is not configured within the bundle. This means that the rest of the object should be empty.
---@field googleSystemId? string System ID of the port on Google's side of the LACP exchange.
---@field neighborSystemId? string System ID of the port on the neighbor's side of the LACP exchange.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkLACPStatusStateEnum "ACTIVE"|"DETACHED"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower
---@field value? number Value of the current receiving or transmitting optical power, read in dBm. Take a known good optical value, give it a 10% margin and trigger warnings relative to that value. In general, a -7dBm warning and a -11dBm alarm are good optical value estimates for most links.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPowerStateEnum The status of the current value when compared to the warning and alarm levels for the receiving or transmitting transceiver. Possible states include: - OK: The value has not crossed a warning threshold. - LOW_WARNING: The value has crossed below the low warning threshold. - HIGH_WARNING: The value has crossed above the high warning threshold. - LOW_ALARM: The value has crossed below the low alarm threshold. - HIGH_ALARM: The value has crossed above the high alarm threshold.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPowerStateEnum "HIGH_ALARM"|"HIGH_WARNING"|"LOW_ALARM"|"LOW_WARNING"|"OK"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatus
---@field lacpStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkLACPStatus
---@field arpCaches? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntryList A list of InterconnectDiagnostics.ARPEntry objects, describing the ARP neighbor entries seen on this link. This will be empty if the link is bundled
---@field macsec? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsMacsecStatus Describes the status of MACsec encryption on this link.
---@field transmittingOpticalPower? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower An InterconnectDiagnostics.LinkOpticalPower object, describing the current value and status of the transmitted light level.
---@field receivingOpticalPower? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower An InterconnectDiagnostics.LinkOpticalPower object, describing the current value and status of the received light level.
---@field googleDemarc? string The Demarc address assigned by Google and provided in the LoA.
---@field circuitId? string The unique ID for this link assigned during turn up by Google.
---@field operationalStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusOperationalStatusEnum The operational status of the link.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatus[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusOperationalStatusEnum "LINK_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_DOWN"|"LINK_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_UP"

---Describes the status of MACsec encryption on the link.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectDiagnosticsMacsecStatus
---@field ckn? string Indicates the Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) currently being used if MACsec is operational.
---@field operational? boolean Indicates whether or not MACsec is operational on this link.

---An interconnect group resource allows customers to create, analyze, and
---expand their redundant connections.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroup
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource type. The server generates this identifier.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field physicalStructure? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupPhysicalStructure
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field interconnects? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupInterconnectMap Interconnects in the InterconnectGroup. Keys are arbitrary user-specified strings. Users are encouraged, but not required, to use their preferred format for resource links as keys. Note that there are add-members and remove-members methods in gcloud. The size of this map is limited by an "Interconnects per group" quota.
---@field etag? string Opaque system-generated token that uniquely identifies the configuration. If provided when patching a configuration in update mode, the provided token must match the current token or the update is rejected. This provides a reliable means of doing read-modify-write (optimistic locking) as described by AIP 154.
---@field configured? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupConfigured
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#InterconnectGroup
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field intent? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupIntent

---[Output Only] The status of the group as configured. This has the same
