---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembers
---@field intentMismatchBehavior? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersIntentMismatchBehaviorEnum|string How to behave when configured.topologyCapability.supportedSLA would not equal intent.topologyCapability after this call.
---@field templateInterconnect? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInput Parameters for the Interconnects to create.
---@field interconnects? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputList

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersIntentMismatchBehaviorEnum "CREATE"|"REJECT"|"UNSPECIFIED"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInput
---@field facility? string A zone-free location to use for all Interconnects created in this call, like "iad-1234".
---@field remoteLocation? string Indicates that this is a Cross-Cloud Interconnect. This field specifies the location outside of Google's network that the interconnect is connected to.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field nocContactEmail? string Email address to contact the customer NOC for operations and maintenance notifications regarding this Interconnect. If specified, this will be used for notifications in addition to all other forms described, such as Cloud Monitoring logs alerting and Cloud Notifications. This field is required for users who sign up for Cloud Interconnect using workforce identity federation.
---@field requestedLinkCount? number Target number of physical links in the link bundle, as requested by the customer.
---@field linkType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputLinkTypeEnum|string Type of link requested, which can take one of the following values: - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_10G_LR: A 10G Ethernet with LR optics - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_100G_LR: A 100G Ethernet with LR optics. - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_400G_LR4: A 400G Ethernet with LR4 optics. Note that this field indicates the speed of each of the links in the bundle, not the speed of the entire bundle.
---@field adminEnabled? boolean Administrative status of the interconnect. When this is set to true, the Interconnect is functional and can carry traffic. When set to false, no packets can be carried over the interconnect and no BGP routes are exchanged over it. By default, the status is set to true.
---@field interconnectType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputInterconnectTypeEnum|string Type of interconnect, which can take one of the following values: - PARTNER: A partner-managed interconnection shared between customers though a partner. - DEDICATED: A dedicated physical interconnection with the customer. Note that a value IT_PRIVATE has been deprecated in favor of DEDICATED.
---@field name? string Name of the Interconnects to be created. This must be specified on the template and/or on each individual interconnect. The name, if not empty, must be 1-63 characters long, and comply with RFC1035. Specifically, any nonempty name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field requestedFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputRequestedFeaturesItemEnumList Optional. List of features requested for this Interconnect connection, which can take one of the following values: - IF_MACSEC: If specified, then the connection is created on MACsec capable hardware ports. If not specified, non-MACsec capable ports will also be considered. - IF_CROSS_SITE_NETWORK: If specified, then the connection is created exclusively for Cross-Site Networking. The connection can not be used for Cross-Site Networking unless this feature is specified.
---@field customerName? string Customer name, to put in the Letter of Authorization as the party authorized to request a crossconnect.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputInterconnectTypeEnum "DEDICATED"|"IT_PRIVATE"|"PARTNER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputLinkTypeEnum "LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_100G_LR"|"LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_10G_LR"|"LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_400G_LR4"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInput[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputRequestedFeaturesItemEnum "IF_CROSS_SITE_NETWORK"|"IF_L2_FORWARDING"|"IF_MACSEC"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputRequestedFeaturesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectGroupsCreateMembersInterconnectInputRequestedFeaturesItemEnum|string)[]

