---Configuration information for enabling Media Access Control security
---(MACsec) on this Cloud Interconnect connection between Google and your
---on-premises router.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsec
---@field preSharedKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKeyList Required. A keychain placeholder describing a set of named key objects along with their start times. A MACsec CKN/CAK is generated for each key in the key chain. Google router automatically picks the key with the most recent startTime when establishing or re-establishing a MACsec secure link.
---@field failOpen? boolean If set to true, the Interconnect connection is configured with ashould-secure MACsec security policy, that allows the Google router to fallback to cleartext traffic if the MKA session cannot be established. By default, the Interconnect connection is configured with amust-secure security policy that drops all traffic if the MKA session cannot be established with your router.
---@field interconnectKeyGroup? string Optional. URL of the InterconnectKeyGroup resource to use for MACsec, in the format: projects/{project}/locations/{region}/interconnectKeyGroups/{interconnectKeyGroup}.

---MACsec configuration information for the Interconnect connection. Contains
---the generated Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) and the key (CAK) for
---this Interconnect connection.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecConfig
---@field preSharedKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKeyList A keychain placeholder describing a set of named key objects along with their start times. A MACsec CKN/CAK is generated for each key in the key chain. Google router automatically picks the key with the most recent startTime when establishing or re-establishing a MACsec secure link.

---Describes a pre-shared key used to setup MACsec in static connectivity
---association key (CAK) mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKey
---@field startTime? string User provided timestamp on or after which this key is valid.
---@field name? string User provided name for this pre-shared key.
---@field ckn? string An auto-generated Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) for this key.
---@field cak? string An auto-generated Connectivity Association Key (CAK) for this key.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKeyList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKey[]

---Describes a pre-shared key used to setup MACsec in static connectivity
---association key (CAK) mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKey
---@field name? string Required. A name for this pre-shared key. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field startTime? string A RFC3339 timestamp on or after which the key is valid. startTime can be in the future. If the keychain has a single key, startTime can be omitted. If the keychain has multiple keys, startTime is mandatory for each key. The start times of keys must be in increasing order. The start times of two consecutive keys must be at least 6 hours apart.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKeyList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKey[]

