---Configuration for location policy among multiple possible locations
---(e.g. preferences for zone selection among zones in a single region).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicy
---@field zones? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyZoneConfigurationList The bulkInsert operation applies any preferences set in the locations field to the specific zones listed in the zones field if the same zones are specified in both fields.
---@field targetShape? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyTargetShapeEnum|string Strategy for distributing VMs across zones in a region.
---@field locations? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationMap Location configurations mapped by location name. Currently only zone names are supported and must be represented as valid internal URLs, such as zones/us-central1-a. The bulkInsert operation doesn't create instances in an AI zone, even if an AI zone is available in the specified region. For example, if you set a DENY preference for us-central1-a, Compute Engine will consider us-central1-b and us-central1-c for instance creation, but not us-central1-ai1a. Also, you can't use the locations[] configuration to allow instance creation in an AI zone. To include an AI zone in bulkInsert operations, use the locationPolicy.zones[] field.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocation
---@field constraints? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationConstraints Constraints that the caller requires on the result distribution in this zone.
---@field preference? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationPreferenceEnum|string Preference for a given location. Set to either ALLOW orDENY.

---Per-zone constraints on location policy for this zone.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationConstraints
---@field maxCount? number Maximum number of items that are allowed to be placed in this zone. The value must be non-negative.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocation }

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyLocationPreferenceEnum "ALLOW"|"DENY"|"PREFERENCE_UNSPECIFIED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyTargetShapeEnum "ANY"|"ANY_SINGLE_ZONE"|"BALANCED"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyZoneConfiguration
---@field zone? string The URL of the zone. The zone must exist in the region where the request is called. Zones must be represented as valid partial URLs, such as zones/us-central1-a.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyZoneConfigurationList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.LocationPolicyZoneConfiguration[]

---Represents a machine image resource.
---
---A machine image is a Compute Engine resource that stores all the
---configuration, metadata, permissions, and data from one or more disks
---required to create a Virtual machine (VM) instance. For more information, seeMachine images.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.MachineImage
---@field machineImageEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.CustomerEncryptionKey Encrypts the machine image using acustomer-supplied encryption key. After you encrypt a machine image using a customer-supplied key, you must provide the same key if you use the machine image later. For example, you must provide the encryption key when you create an instance from the encrypted machine image in a future request. Customer-supplied encryption keys do not protect access to metadata of the machine image. If you do not provide an encryption key when creating the machine image, then the machine image will be encrypted using an automatically generated key and you do not need to provide a key to use the machine image later.
---@field guestFlush? boolean [Input Only] Whether to attempt an application consistent machine image by informing the OS to prepare for the snapshot process.
---@field totalStorageBytes? string Output only. [Output Only] Total size of the storage used by the machine image.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] The creation timestamp for this machine image inRFC3339 text format.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] The URL for this machine image. The server defines this URL.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field instanceProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceProperties [Output Only] Properties of source instance
---@field sourceInstanceProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SourceInstanceProperties Output only. [Output Only] DEPRECATED: Please use instance_properties instead for source instance related properties. New properties will not be added to this field.
---@field sourceInstance? string The source instance used to create the machine image. You can provide this as a partial or full URL to the resource. For example, the following are valid values: - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/zones/zone/instances/instance - projects/project/zones/zone/instances/instance
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] A unique identifier for this machine image. The server defines this identifier.
---@field labelFingerprint? string A fingerprint for the labels being applied to this machine image, which is essentially a hash of the labels set used for optimistic locking. The fingerprint is initially generated by Compute Engine and changes after every request to modify or update labels. You must always provide an up-to-date fingerprint hash in order to update or change labels. To see the latest fingerprint, make get() request to the machine image.
---@field name? string Name of the resource; provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field sourceDiskEncryptionKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SourceDiskEncryptionKeyList [Input Only] Thecustomer-supplied encryption key of the disks attached to the source instance. Required if the source disk is protected by a customer-supplied encryption key.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Labels to apply to this machine image. These can be later modified by the setLabels method.
---@field savedDisks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SavedDiskList Output only. An array of Machine Image specific properties for disks attached to the source instance
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.MachineImageStatusEnum Output only. [Output Only] The status of the machine image. One of the following values:INVALID, CREATING, READY,DELETING, and UPLOADING.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.MachineImageParams Input only. [Input Only] Additional parameters that are passed in the request, but are not persisted in the resource.
---@field storageLocations? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList The regional or multi-regional Cloud Storage bucket location where themachine image is stored.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] The resource type, which is alwayscompute#machineImage for machine image.

