---A public advertised prefix represents an aggregated IP prefix or netblock
---which customers bring to cloud. The IP prefix is a single unit of route
---advertisement and is announced globally to the internet.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefix
---@field byoipApiVersion? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixByoipApiVersionEnum Output only. [Output Only] The version of BYOIP API.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#publicAdvertisedPrefix for public advertised prefixes.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field networkTier? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixNetworkTierEnum Network tier to be used for this prefix. All child delegated prefixes will inherit this field. If this field is not specified, it defaults to the network tier of the project that the PublicAdvertisedPrefix belongs to.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource type. The server generates this identifier.
---@field publicDelegatedPrefixs? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixPublicDelegatedPrefixList Output only. [Output Only] The list of public delegated prefixes that exist for this public advertised prefix.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixStatusEnum The status of the public advertised prefix. Possible values include: - `INITIAL`: RPKI validation is complete. - `PTR_CONFIGURED`: User has configured the PTR. - `VALIDATED`: Reverse DNS lookup is successful. - `REVERSE_DNS_LOOKUP_FAILED`: Reverse DNS lookup failed. - `PREFIX_CONFIGURATION_IN_PROGRESS`: The prefix is being configured. - `PREFIX_CONFIGURATION_COMPLETE`: The prefix is fully configured. - `PREFIX_REMOVAL_IN_PROGRESS`: The prefix is being removed.
---@field fingerprint? string Fingerprint of this resource. A hash of the contents stored in this object. This field is used in optimistic locking. This field will be ignored when inserting a new PublicAdvertisedPrefix. An up-to-date fingerprint must be provided in order to update thePublicAdvertisedPrefix, otherwise the request will fail with error 412 conditionNotMet. To see the latest fingerprint, make a get() request to retrieve a PublicAdvertisedPrefix.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field ipv6AccessType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixIpv6AccessTypeEnum The internet access type for IPv6 Public Advertised Prefixes.
---@field dnsVerificationIp? string The address to be used for reverse DNS verification.
---@field pdpScope? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixPdpScopeEnum Specifies how child public delegated prefix will be scoped. It could be one of following values: - `REGIONAL`: The public delegated prefix is regional only. The provisioning will take a few minutes. - `GLOBAL`: The public delegated prefix is global only. The provisioning will take ~4 weeks. - `GLOBAL_AND_REGIONAL` [output only]: The public delegated prefixes is BYOIP V1 legacy prefix. This is output only value and no longer supported in BYOIP V2.
---@field sharedSecret? string [Output Only] The shared secret to be used for reverse DNS verification.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field ipCidrRange? string The address range, in CIDR format, represented by this public advertised prefix.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixByoipApiVersionEnum "V1"|"V2"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.PublicAdvertisedPrefixIpv6AccessTypeEnum "EXTERNAL"|"INTERNAL"

