---Represents a reservation resource.  A reservation ensures that capacity is
---held in a specific zone even if the reserved VMs are not running. For more
---information, read  Reserving zonal
---resources.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Reservation
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#reservations for reservations.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field deleteAtTime? string Absolute time in future when the reservation will be auto-deleted by Compute Engine. Timestamp is represented inRFC3339 text format.
---@field linkedCommitments? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. [Output Only] Full or partial URL to parent commitments. This field displays for reservations that are tied to multiple commitments.
---@field earlyAccessMaintenance? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationEarlyAccessMaintenanceEnum|string Indicates the early access maintenance for the reservation. If this field is absent or set to NO_EARLY_ACCESS, the reservation is not enrolled in early access maintenance and the standard notice applies.
---@field advancedDeploymentControl? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControl Advanced control for cluster management, applicable only to DENSE deployment type reservations.
---@field shareSettings? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShareSettings Specify share-settings to create a shared reservation. This property is optional. For more information about the syntax and options for this field and its subfields, see the guide for creating a shared reservation.
---@field specificReservationRequired? boolean Indicates whether the reservation can be consumed by VMs with affinity for "any" reservation. If the field is set, then only VMs that target the reservation by name can consume from this reservation.
---@field enableEmergentMaintenance? boolean Indicates whether Compute Engine allows unplanned maintenance for your VMs; for example, to fix hardware errors.
---@field reservationMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationReservationModeEnum|string Output only. [Output only] Indicates the reservation mode of the reservation.
---@field aggregateReservation? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AllocationAggregateReservation Reservation for aggregated resources, providing shape flexibility.
---@field protectionTier? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationProtectionTierEnum|string Protection tier for the workload which specifies the workload expectations in the event of infrastructure failures at data center (e.g. power and/or cooling failures).
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Resource policies to be added to this reservation. The key is defined by user, and the value is resource policy url. This is to define placement policy with reservation.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationParams Input only. Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationStatusEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The status of the reservation. - CREATING: Reservation resources are being allocated. - READY: Reservation resources have been allocated, and the reservation is ready for use. - DELETING: Reservation deletion is in progress. - UPDATING: Reservation update is in progress.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined fully-qualified URL for this resource.
---@field resourceStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AllocationResourceStatus Output only. [Output Only] Status information for Reservation resource.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field zone? string Zone in which the reservation resides. A zone must be provided if the reservation is created within a commitment.
---@field specificReservation? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AllocationSpecificSKUReservation Reservation for instances with specific machine shapes.
---@field schedulingType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationSchedulingTypeEnum|string The type of maintenance for the reservation.
---@field reservationSharingPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AllocationReservationSharingPolicy Specify the reservation sharing policy. If unspecified, the reservation will not be shared with Google Cloud managed services.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field deleteAfterDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Duration time relative to reservation creation when Compute Engine will automatically delete this resource.
---@field confidentialComputeType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationConfidentialComputeTypeEnum|string
---@field deploymentType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ReservationDeploymentTypeEnum|string Specifies the deployment strategy for this reservation.
---@field commitment? string Output only. [Output Only] Full or partial URL to a parent commitment. This field displays for reservations that are tied to a commitment.

