---@field value? string [Output Only] A warning data value corresponding to the key.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterAggregatedListWarningDataItemList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterAggregatedListWarningDataItem[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgp
---@field identifierRange? string Explicitly specifies a range of valid BGP Identifiers for this Router. It is provided as a link-local IPv4 range (from 169.254.0.0/16), of size at least /30, even if the BGP sessions are over IPv6. It must not overlap with any IPv4 BGP session ranges. Other vendors commonly call this "router ID".
---@field keepaliveInterval? number The interval in seconds between BGP keepalive messages that are sent to the peer. Hold time is three times the interval at which keepalive messages are sent, and the hold time is the maximum number of seconds allowed to elapse between successive keepalive messages that BGP receives from a peer. BGP will use the smaller of either the local hold time value or the peer's hold time value as the hold time for the BGP connection between the two peers. If set, this value must be between 20 and 60. The default is 20.
---@field advertisedGroups? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertisedGroupsItemEnumList User-specified list of prefix groups to advertise in custom mode. This field can only be populated if advertise_mode is CUSTOM and is advertised to all peers of the router. These groups will be advertised in addition to any specified prefixes. Leave this field blank to advertise no custom groups.
---@field asn? number Local BGP Autonomous System Number (ASN). Must be anRFC6996 private ASN, either 16-bit or 32-bit. The value will be fixed for this router resource. All VPN tunnels that link to this router will have the same local ASN.
---@field advertiseMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertiseModeEnum|string User-specified flag to indicate which mode to use for advertisement. The options are DEFAULT or CUSTOM.
---@field advertisedIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterAdvertisedIpRangeList User-specified list of individual IP ranges to advertise in custom mode. This field can only be populated if advertise_mode is CUSTOM and is advertised to all peers of the router. These IP ranges will be advertised in addition to any specified groups. Leave this field blank to advertise no custom IP ranges.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertiseModeEnum "CUSTOM"|"DEFAULT"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertisedGroupsItemEnum "ALL_SUBNETS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertisedGroupsItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpAdvertisedGroupsItemEnum|string)[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeer
---@field bfd? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerBfd BFD configuration for the BGP peering.
---@field linkedCustomHardware? string The linked custom hardware resource. The URI of the custom hardware link attachment is where you will establish the BGP session from the Cloud Router. This link attachment must reside in the same subnetwork as the associated router interface.
---@field interfaceName? string Name of the interface the BGP peer is associated with.
---@field name? string Name of this BGP peer. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field exportPolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList List of export policies applied to this peer, in the order they must be evaluated. The name must correspond to an existing policy that has ROUTE_POLICY_TYPE_EXPORT type.
---@field enableIpv6? boolean Enable IPv6 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 6.
---@field enableIpv4? boolean Enable IPv4 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 4.
---@field enable? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerEnableEnum|string The status of the BGP peer connection. If set to FALSE, any active session with the peer is terminated and all associated routing information is removed. If set to TRUE, the peer connection can be established with routing information. The default is TRUE.
---@field customLearnedRoutePriority? number The user-defined custom learned route priority for a BGP session. This value is applied to all custom learned route ranges for the session. You can choose a value from `0` to `65335`. If you don't provide a value, Google Cloud assigns a priority of `100` to the ranges.
---@field advertiseMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertiseModeEnum|string User-specified flag to indicate which mode to use for advertisement.
---@field managementType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerManagementTypeEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The resource that configures and manages this BGP peer. - MANAGED_BY_USER is the default value and can be managed by you or other users - MANAGED_BY_ATTACHMENT is a BGP peer that is configured and managed by Cloud Interconnect, specifically by an InterconnectAttachment of type PARTNER. Google automatically creates, updates, and deletes this type of BGP peer when the PARTNER InterconnectAttachment is created, updated, or deleted.
---@field peerIpv6NexthopAddress? string IPv6 address of the BGP interface outside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field ipAddress? string IP address of the interface inside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field advertisedGroups? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertisedGroupsItemEnumList User-specified list of prefix groups to advertise in custom mode, which currently supports the following option: - ALL_SUBNETS: Advertises all of the router's own VPC subnets. This excludes any routes learned for subnets that use VPC Network Peering. Note that this field can only be populated if advertise_mode is CUSTOM and overrides the list defined for the router (in the "bgp" message). These groups are advertised in addition to any specified prefixes. Leave this field blank to advertise no custom groups.
---@field routerApplianceInstance? string URI of the VM instance that is used as third-party router appliances such as Next Gen Firewalls, Virtual Routers, or Router Appliances. The VM instance must be located in zones contained in the same region as this Cloud Router. The VM instance is the peer side of the BGP session.
---@field md5AuthenticationKeyName? string Present if MD5 authentication is enabled for the peering. Must be the name of one of the entries in the Router.md5_authentication_keys. The field must comply with RFC1035.
---@field advertisedIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterAdvertisedIpRangeList User-specified list of individual IP ranges to advertise in custom mode. This field can only be populated if advertise_mode is CUSTOM and overrides the list defined for the router (in the "bgp" message). These IP ranges are advertised in addition to any specified groups. Leave this field blank to advertise no custom IP ranges.
---@field ipv4NexthopAddress? string IPv4 address of the interface inside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field peerIpv4NexthopAddress? string IPv4 address of the BGP interface outside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field advertisedRoutePriority? number The priority of routes advertised to this BGP peer. Where there is more than one matching route of maximum length, the routes with the lowest priority value win.
---@field importPolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList List of import policies applied to this peer, in the order they must be evaluated. The name must correspond to an existing policy that has ROUTE_POLICY_TYPE_IMPORT type.
---@field peerAsn? number Peer BGP Autonomous System Number (ASN). Each BGP interface may use a different value.
---@field peerIpAddress? string IP address of the BGP interface outside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field ipv6NexthopAddress? string IPv6 address of the interface inside Google Cloud Platform.
---@field customLearnedIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerCustomLearnedIpRangeList A list of user-defined custom learned route IP address ranges for a BGP session.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertiseModeEnum "CUSTOM"|"DEFAULT"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertisedGroupsItemEnum "ALL_SUBNETS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertisedGroupsItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerAdvertisedGroupsItemEnum|string)[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerBfd
---@field sessionInitializationMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerBfdSessionInitializationModeEnum|string The BFD session initialization mode for this BGP peer. If set to ACTIVE, the Cloud Router will initiate the BFD session for this BGP peer. If set to PASSIVE, the Cloud Router will wait for the peer router to initiate the BFD session for this BGP peer. If set to DISABLED, BFD is disabled for this BGP peer. The default is DISABLED.
---@field minReceiveInterval? number The minimum interval, in milliseconds, between BFD control packets received from the peer router. The actual value is negotiated between the two routers and is equal to the greater of this value and the transmit interval of the other router. If set, this value must be between 1000 and 30000. The default is 1000.
---@field minTransmitInterval? number The minimum interval, in milliseconds, between BFD control packets transmitted to the peer router. The actual value is negotiated between the two routers and is equal to the greater of this value and the corresponding receive interval of the other router. If set, this value must be between 1000 and 30000. The default is 1000.
---@field multiplier? number The number of consecutive BFD packets that must be missed before BFD declares that a peer is unavailable. If set, the value must be a value between 5 and 16. The default is 5.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerBfdSessionInitializationModeEnum "ACTIVE"|"DISABLED"|"PASSIVE"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerCustomLearnedIpRange
---@field range? string The custom learned route IP address range. Must be a valid CIDR-formatted prefix. If an IP address is provided without a subnet mask, it is interpreted as, for IPv4, a `/32` singular IP address range, and, for IPv6, `/128`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerCustomLearnedIpRangeList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerCustomLearnedIpRange[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerEnableEnum "FALSE"|"TRUE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeer[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterBgpPeerManagementTypeEnum "MANAGED_BY_ATTACHMENT"|"MANAGED_BY_USER"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterface
---@field managementType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterfaceManagementTypeEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The resource that configures and manages this interface. - MANAGED_BY_USER is the default value and can be managed directly by users. - MANAGED_BY_ATTACHMENT is an interface that is configured and managed by Cloud Interconnect, specifically, by an InterconnectAttachment of type PARTNER. Google automatically creates, updates, and deletes this type of interface when the PARTNER InterconnectAttachment is created, updated, or deleted.
---@field ipVersion? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterfaceIpVersionEnum|string IP version of this interface.
---@field ipRange? string IP address and range of the interface. - For Internet Protocol version 4 (IPv4), the IP range must be in theRFC3927 link-local IP address space. The value must be a CIDR-formatted string, for example, 169.254.0.1/30. Note: Do not truncate the IP address, as it represents the IP address of the interface. - For Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6), the value must be a unique local address (ULA) range from fdff:1::/64 with a mask length of 126 or less. This value should be a CIDR-formatted string, for example, fdff:1::1/112. Within the router's VPC, this IPv6 prefix will be reserved exclusively for this connection and cannot be used for any other purpose.
---@field linkedVpnTunnel? string URI of the linked VPN tunnel, which must be in the same region as the router. Each interface can have one linked resource, which can be a VPN tunnel, an Interconnect attachment, or a subnetwork.
---@field redundantInterface? string Name of the interface that will be redundant with the current interface you are creating. The redundantInterface must belong to the same Cloud Router as the interface here. To establish the BGP session to a Router Appliance VM, you must create two BGP peers. The two BGP peers must be attached to two separate interfaces that are redundant with each other. The redundant_interface must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the redundant_interface must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field linkedInterconnectAttachment? string URI of the linked Interconnect attachment. It must be in the same region as the router. Each interface can have one linked resource, which can be a VPN tunnel, an Interconnect attachment, or a subnetwork.
---@field name? string Name of this interface entry. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field privateIpAddress? string The regional private internal IP address that is used to establish BGP sessions to a VM instance acting as a third-party Router Appliance, such as a Next Gen Firewall, a Virtual Router, or an SD-WAN VM.
---@field subnetwork? string The URI of the subnetwork resource that this interface belongs to, which must be in the same region as the Cloud Router. When you establish a BGP session to a VM instance using this interface, the VM instance must belong to the same subnetwork as the subnetwork specified here.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterfaceIpVersionEnum "IPV4"|"IPV6"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterfaceList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterface[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterInterfaceManagementTypeEnum "MANAGED_BY_ATTACHMENT"|"MANAGED_BY_USER"

---Contains a list of Router resources.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterList
---@field warning? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarning [Output Only] Informational warning message.
---@field items gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterList_ A list of Router resources.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of resource. Always compute#router for routers.
---@field nextPageToken? string [Output Only] This token allows you to get the next page of results for list requests. If the number of results is larger thanmaxResults, use the nextPageToken as a value for the query parameter pageToken in the next list request. Subsequent list requests will have their own nextPageToken to continue paging through the results.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource.
---@field id? string [Output Only] Unique identifier for the resource; defined by the server.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarning
---@field data? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningDataItemList [Output Only] Metadata about this warning in key: value format. For example: "data": [ { "key": "scope", "value": "zones/us-east1-d" }]
---@field message? string [Output Only] A human-readable description of the warning code.
---@field code? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningCodeEnum [Output Only] A warning code, if applicable. For example, Compute Engine returns NO_RESULTS_ON_PAGE if there are no results in the response.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningCodeEnum "CLEANUP_FAILED"|"DEPRECATED_RESOURCE_USED"|"DEPRECATED_TYPE_USED"|"DISK_SIZE_LARGER_THAN_IMAGE_SIZE"|"EXPERIMENTAL_TYPE_USED"|"EXTERNAL_API_WARNING"|"FIELD_VALUE_OVERRIDEN"|"INJECTED_KERNELS_DEPRECATED"|"INVALID_HEALTH_CHECK_FOR_DYNAMIC_WIEGHTED_LB"|"LARGE_DEPLOYMENT_WARNING"|"LIST_OVERHEAD_QUOTA_EXCEED"|"MISSING_TYPE_DEPENDENCY"|"NEXT_HOP_ADDRESS_NOT_ASSIGNED"|"NEXT_HOP_CANNOT_IP_FORWARD"|"NEXT_HOP_INSTANCE_HAS_NO_IPV6_INTERFACE"|"NEXT_HOP_INSTANCE_NOT_FOUND"|"NEXT_HOP_INSTANCE_NOT_ON_NETWORK"|"NEXT_HOP_NOT_RUNNING"|"NOT_CRITICAL_ERROR"|"NO_RESULTS_ON_PAGE"|"PARTIAL_SUCCESS"|"QUOTA_INFO_UNAVAILABLE"|"REQUIRED_TOS_AGREEMENT"|"RESOURCE_IN_USE_BY_OTHER_RESOURCE_WARNING"|"RESOURCE_NOT_DELETED"|"SCHEMA_VALIDATION_IGNORED"|"SINGLE_INSTANCE_PROPERTY_TEMPLATE"|"UNDECLARED_PROPERTIES"|"UNREACHABLE"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningDataItem
---@field key? string [Output Only] A key that provides more detail on the warning being returned. For example, for warnings where there are no results in a list request for a particular zone, this key might be scope and the key value might be the zone name. Other examples might be a key indicating a deprecated resource and a suggested replacement, or a warning about invalid network settings (for example, if an instance attempts to perform IP forwarding but is not enabled for IP forwarding).
---@field value? string [Output Only] A warning data value corresponding to the key.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningDataItemList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterListWarningDataItem[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterList_ gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Router[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterMd5AuthenticationKey
---@field key? string [Input only] Value of the key. For patch and update calls, it can be skipped to copy the value from the previous configuration. This is allowed if the key with the same name existed before the operation. Maximum length is 80 characters. Can only contain printable ASCII characters.
---@field name? string Name used to identify the key. Must be unique within a router. Must be referenced by exactly one bgpPeer. Must comply withRFC1035.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterMd5AuthenticationKeyList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterMd5AuthenticationKey[]

---Represents a Nat resource. It enables the VMs within the specified
---subnetworks to access Internet without external IP addresses. It specifies
---a list of subnetworks (and the ranges within) that want to use NAT.
---Customers can also provide the external IPs that would be used for NAT. GCP
---would auto-allocate ephemeral IPs if no external IPs are provided.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNat
---@field enableEndpointIndependentMapping? boolean
---@field name? string Unique name of this Nat service. The name must be 1-63 characters long and comply withRFC1035.
---@field udpIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for UDP connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field natIpAllocateOption? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatNatIpAllocateOptionEnum|string Specify the NatIpAllocateOption, which can take one of the following values: - MANUAL_ONLY: Uses only Nat IP addresses provided by customers. When there are not enough specified Nat IPs, the Nat service fails for new VMs. - AUTO_ONLY: Nat IPs are allocated by Google Cloud Platform; customers can't specify any Nat IPs. When choosing AUTO_ONLY, then nat_ip should be empty.
---@field tcpEstablishedIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP established connections. Defaults to 1200s if not set.
---@field autoNetworkTier? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatAutoNetworkTierEnum|string The network tier to use when automatically reserving NAT IP addresses. Must be one of: PREMIUM, STANDARD. If not specified, then the current project-level default tier is used.
---@field tcpTransitoryIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP transitory connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field minPortsPerVm? number Minimum number of ports allocated to a VM from this NAT config. If not set, a default number of ports is allocated to a VM. This is rounded up to the nearest power of 2. For example, if the value of this field is 50, at least 64 ports are allocated to a VM.
---@field sourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNatEnum|string Specify the Nat option, which can take one of the following values: - ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES: All of the IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_PRIMARY_IP_RANGES: All of the primary IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS: A list of Subnetworks are allowed to Nat (specified in the field subnetwork below) The default is SUBNETWORK_IP_RANGE_TO_NAT_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. Note that if this field contains ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES then there should not be any other Router.Nat section in any Router for this network in this region.
---@field effectiveTcpTimeWaitTimeoutSec? number Output only. Effective timeout (in seconds) for TCP connections that are in TIME_WAIT state. This value is equal to tcp_time_wait_timeout_sec. If tcp_time_wait_timeout_sec isn't set, the effective timeout is 30s or 120s. The field is output only.
---@field enableDynamicPortAllocation? boolean Enable Dynamic Port Allocation. If not specified, it is disabled by default. If set to true, - Dynamic Port Allocation will be enabled on this NAT config. - enableEndpointIndependentMapping cannot be set to true. - If minPorts is set, minPortsPerVm must be set to a power of two greater than or equal to 32. If minPortsPerVm is not set, a minimum of 32 ports will be allocated to a VM from this NAT config.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatTypeEnum|string Indicates whether this NAT is used for public or private IP translation. If unspecified, it defaults to PUBLIC.
---@field nat64Subnetworks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64List List of Subnetwork resources whose traffic should be translated by NAT64 Gateway. It is used only when LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS is selected for the SubnetworkIpRangeToNat64Option above.
---@field logConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatLogConfig Configure logging on this NAT.
---@field rules? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRuleList A list of rules associated with this NAT.
---@field subnetworks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatList A list of Subnetwork resources whose traffic should be translated by NAT Gateway. It is used only when LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS is selected for the SubnetworkIpRangeToNatOption above.
---@field natIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources used for this Nat service. These IP addresses must be valid static external IP addresses assigned to the project.
---@field sourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64Enum|string Specify the Nat option for NAT64, which can take one of the following values: - ALL_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS: All of the IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS: A list of Subnetworks are allowed to Nat (specified in the field nat64_subnetwork below) The default is NAT64_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. Note that if this field contains NAT64_ALL_V6_SUBNETWORKS no other Router.Nat section in this region can also enable NAT64 for any Subnetworks in this network. Other Router.Nat sections can still be present to enable NAT44 only.
---@field drainNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources to be drained. These IPs must be valid static external IPs that have been assigned to the NAT. These IPs should be used for updating/patching a NAT only.
---@field tcpTimeWaitTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP connections that are in TIME_WAIT state. Defaults to 120s if not set.
---@field icmpIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for ICMP connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field endpointTypes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnumList List of NAT-ted endpoint types supported by the Nat Gateway. If the list is empty, then it will be equivalent to include ENDPOINT_TYPE_VM
---@field maxPortsPerVm? number Maximum number of ports allocated to a VM from this NAT config when Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled. If Dynamic Port Allocation is not enabled, this field has no effect. If Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled, and this field is set, it must be set to a power of two greater than minPortsPerVm, or 64 if minPortsPerVm is not set. If Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled and this field is not set, a maximum of 65536 ports will be allocated to a VM from this NAT config.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatAutoNetworkTierEnum "FIXED_STANDARD"|"PREMIUM"|"STANDARD"|"STANDARD_OVERRIDES_FIXED_STANDARD"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnum "ENDPOINT_TYPE_MANAGED_PROXY_LB"|"ENDPOINT_TYPE_SWG"|"ENDPOINT_TYPE_VM"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNat[]

---Configuration of logging on a NAT.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatLogConfig
---@field enable? boolean Indicates whether or not to export logs. This is false by default.
---@field filter? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatLogConfigFilterEnum|string Specify the desired filtering of logs on this NAT. If unspecified, logs are exported for all connections handled by this NAT. This option can take one of the following values: - ERRORS_ONLY: Export logs only for connection failures. - TRANSLATIONS_ONLY: Export logs only for successful connections. - ALL: Export logs for all connections, successful and unsuccessful.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatLogConfigFilterEnum "ALL"|"ERRORS_ONLY"|"TRANSLATIONS_ONLY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatNatIpAllocateOptionEnum "AUTO_ONLY"|"MANUAL_ONLY"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRule
---@field description? string An optional description of this rule.
---@field ruleNumber? number An integer uniquely identifying a rule in the list. The rule number must be a positive value between 0 and 65000, and must be unique among rules within a NAT.
---@field sourceWorkloadIdentities? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of source workload identities.
---@field match? string CEL expression that specifies the match condition that egress traffic from a VM is evaluated against. If it evaluates to true, the corresponding `action` is enforced. The following examples are valid match expressions for public NAT: `inIpRange(destination.ip, '1.1.0.0/16') || inIpRange(destination.ip, '2.2.0.0/16')` `destination.ip == '1.1.0.1' || destination.ip == '8.8.8.8'` The following examples are valid match expressions for private NAT: (NAT 44) `nexthop.hub == '//networkconnectivity.googleapis.com/projects/my-project/locations/global/hubs/hub-1'` `nexthop.is_hybrid` (NAT 64) `isIPv6(source.ip)`
---@field action? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRuleAction The action to be enforced for traffic that matches this rule.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRuleAction
---@field sourceNatActiveIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources used for this NAT rule. These IP addresses must be valid static external IP addresses assigned to the project. This field is used for public NAT.
---@field sourceNatDrainRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of subnetworks representing source ranges to be drained. This is only supported on patch/update, and these subnetworks must have previously been used as active ranges in this NAT Rule. This field is used for private NAT.
---@field sourceNatActiveRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of the subnetworks used as source ranges for this NAT Rule. These subnetworks must have purpose set to PRIVATE_NAT. This field is used for private NAT.
---@field sourceNatDrainIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources to be drained. These IPs must be valid static external IPs that have been assigned to the NAT. These IPs should be used for updating/patching a NAT rule only. This field is used for public NAT.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRuleList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatRule[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64Enum "ALL_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS"|"LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNatEnum "ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES"|"ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_PRIMARY_IP_RANGES"|"LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS"

---Defines the IP ranges that want to use NAT for a subnetwork.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat
---@field name? string URL for the subnetwork resource that will use NAT.
---@field sourceIpRangesToNat? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnumList Specify the options for NAT ranges in the Subnetwork. All options of a single value are valid except NAT_IP_RANGE_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. The only valid option with multiple values is: ["PRIMARY_IP_RANGE", "LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES"] Default: [ALL_IP_RANGES]
---@field secondaryIpRangeNames? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of the secondary ranges of the Subnetwork that are allowed to use NAT. This can be populated only if "LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES" is one of the values in source_ip_ranges_to_nat.

---Specifies a subnetwork to enable NAT64.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64
---@field name? string URL for the subnetwork resource that will use NAT64.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64List gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnum "ALL_IP_RANGES"|"LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES"|"PRIMARY_IP_RANGE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterNatTypeEnum "PRIVATE"|"PUBLIC"

---Additional router parameters.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterParams
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Tag keys/values directly bound to this resource. The field is allowed for INSERT only. The keys/values to set on the resource should be specified in either ID { : } or Namespaced format { : }. For example the following are valid inputs: * {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "tagKeys/123" : "tagValues/456"} * {"123/environment" : "production", "345/abc" : "xyz"} Note: * Invalid combinations of ID & namespaced format is not supported. For instance: {"123/environment" : "tagValues/444"} is invalid. * Inconsistent format is not supported. For instance: {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "123/env" : "prod"} is invalid.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatus
---@field natStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatusList
---@field bestRoutesForRouter? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouteList_ A list of the best BGP routes learned by this Cloud Router. It is possible that routes listed might not be programmed into the data plane, if the Google Cloud control plane finds a more optimal route for a prefix than a route learned by this Cloud Router.
---@field network? string URI of the network to which this router belongs.
---@field bgpPeerStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusList
---@field nccGateway? string URI of the ncc_gateway to which this router associated.
---@field bestRoutes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouteList_ A list of the best dynamic routes for this Cloud Router's Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) network in the same region as this Cloud Router. Lists all of the best routes per prefix that are programmed into this region's VPC data plane. When global dynamic routing mode is turned on in the VPC network, this list can include cross-region dynamic routes from Cloud Routers in other regions.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatus
---@field ipAddress? string Output only. IP address of the local BGP interface.
---@field numLearnedRoutes? number Output only. Number of routes learned from the remote BGP Peer.
---@field state? string Output only. The state of the BGP session. For a list of possible values for this field, seeBGP session states.
---@field peerIpAddress? string Output only. IP address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field bfdStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BfdStatus
---@field ipv6NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv6 address of the local BGP interface.
---@field enableIpv4? boolean Output only. Enable IPv4 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 4.
---@field linkedCustomHardware? string Output only. The URI of the linked custom hardware resource, CustomHardwareLinkAttachment. This CustomHardwareLinkAttachment resource is the one that will establish the BGP session from the Cloud Router.
---@field peerIpv4NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv4 address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field md5AuthEnabled? boolean Informs whether MD5 authentication is enabled on this BGP peer.
---@field depreferenced? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Indicates whether the BGP peer is in a depreferenced state.
---@field routerApplianceInstance? string Output only. [Output only] URI of the VM instance that is used as third-party router appliances such as Next Gen Firewalls, Virtual Routers, or Router Appliances. The VM instance is the peer side of the BGP session.
---@field ipv4NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv4 address of the local BGP interface.
---@field uptimeSeconds? string Output only. Time this session has been up, in seconds. Format: 145
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusEnum Output only. Status of the BGP peer: {UP, DOWN}
---@field advertisedRoutes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouteList_ Routes that were advertised to the remote BGP peer
---@field enableIpv6? boolean Output only. Enable IPv6 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 6.
---@field peerIpv6NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv6 address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field uptime? string Output only. Time this session has been up. Format: 14 years, 51 weeks, 6 days, 23 hours, 59 minutes, 59 seconds
---@field statusReason? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusReasonEnum Indicates why particular status was returned.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of this BGP peer. Unique within the Routers resource.
---@field linkedVpnTunnel? string Output only. URL of the VPN tunnel that this BGP peer controls.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatus[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusEnum "DOWN"|"UNKNOWN"|"UP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusReasonEnum "IPV4_PEER_ON_IPV6_ONLY_CONNECTION"|"IPV6_PEER_ON_IPV4_ONLY_CONNECTION"|"MD5_AUTH_INTERNAL_PROBLEM"|"STATUS_REASON_UNSPECIFIED"

---Status of a NAT contained in this router.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatus
---@field name? string Output only. Unique name of this NAT.
---@field ruleStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatusList Status of rules in this NAT.
---@field userAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of IPs user-allocated for NAT. They will be raw IP strings like "179.12.26.133".
---@field minExtraNatIpsNeeded? number Output only. The number of extra IPs to allocate. This will be greater than 0 only if user-specified IPs are NOT enough to allow all configured VMs to use NAT. This value is meaningful only when auto-allocation of NAT IPs is *not* used.
---@field drainUserAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of IPs user-allocated for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field drainAutoAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of IPs auto-allocated for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field numVmEndpointsWithNatMappings? number Output only. Number of VM endpoints (i.e., Nics) that can use NAT.
---@field userAllocatedNatIpResources? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of fully qualified URLs of reserved IP address resources.
---@field autoAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of IPs auto-allocated for NAT. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "129.2.16.89"]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatus[]

---Status of a NAT Rule contained in this NAT.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatus
---@field ruleNumber? number Output only. Rule number of the rule.
---@field drainNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Output only. A list of IPs for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
