---Sets the scheduling options for an Instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Scheduling
---@field preemptionNoticeDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Specifies the Metadata Service preemption notice duration before the GCE ACPI G2 Soft Off signal is triggered for Spot VMs only. If not specified, there will be no wait before the G2 Soft Off signal is triggered.
---@field nodeAffinities? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingNodeAffinityList A set of node affinity and anti-affinity configurations. Refer toConfiguring node affinity for more information. Overrides reservationAffinity.
---@field preemptible? boolean Defines whether the instance is preemptible. This can only be set during instance creation or while the instance isstopped and therefore, in a `TERMINATED` state. SeeInstance Life Cycle for more information on the possible instance states.
---@field maintenanceFreezeDurationHours? number Specifies the number of hours after VM instance creation where the VM won't be scheduled for maintenance.
---@field availabilityDomain? number Specifies the availability domain to place the instance in. The value must be a number between 1 and the number of availability domains specified in the spread placement policy attached to the instance.
---@field maxRunDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Specifies the max run duration for the given instance. If specified, the instance termination action will be performed at the end of the run duration.
---@field exposeHostTopology? boolean This optional flag exposes the hashed physical host ID in the ResourceStatus resource of the VM.
---@field maintenanceInterval? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingMaintenanceIntervalEnum|string Specifies the frequency of planned maintenance events. The accepted values are: `PERIODIC`.
---@field gracefulShutdown? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingGracefulShutdown
---@field provisioningModel? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingProvisioningModelEnum|string Specifies the provisioning model of the instance.
---@field hostErrorTimeoutSeconds? number Specify the time in seconds for host error detection, the value must be within the range of [90, 330] with the increment of 30, if unset, the default behavior of host error recovery will be used.
---@field localSsdRecoveryTimeout? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration Specifies the maximum amount of time a Local Ssd Vm should wait while recovery of the Local Ssd state is attempted. Its value should be in between 0 and 168 hours with hour granularity and the default value being 1 hour.
---@field automaticRestart? boolean Specifies whether the instance should be automatically restarted if it is terminated by Compute Engine (not terminated by a user). You can only set the automatic restart option for standard instances.Preemptible instances cannot be automatically restarted. By default, this is set to true so an instance is automatically restarted if it is terminated by Compute Engine.
---@field locationHint? string An opaque location hint used to place the instance close to other resources. This field is for use by internal tools that use the public API.
---@field terminationTime? string Specifies the timestamp, when the instance will be terminated, inRFC3339 text format. If specified, the instance termination action will be performed at the termination time.
---@field skipGuestOsShutdown? boolean Defines whether GCE ACPI G2 Soft Off signal should be skipped during shutdown operation of VM. Default is false, meaning there will be 120 seconds between GCE ACPI G2 Soft Off and ACPI G3 Mechanical Off for Standard VMs and 30 seconds for Spot VMs.
---@field minNodeCpus? number The minimum number of virtual CPUs this instance will consume when running on a sole-tenant node.
---@field instanceTerminationAction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingInstanceTerminationActionEnum|string Specifies the termination action for the instance.
---@field onInstanceStopAction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingOnInstanceStopAction
---@field onHostMaintenance? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingOnHostMaintenanceEnum|string Defines the maintenance behavior for this instance. For standard instances, the default behavior is MIGRATE. Forpreemptible instances, the default and only possible behavior is TERMINATE. For more information, see Set VM host maintenance policy.

---The configuration for gracefully shutting down the instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingGracefulShutdown
---@field maxDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Duration The time allotted for the instance to gracefully shut down. If the graceful shutdown isn't complete after this time, then the instance transitions to the STOPPING state.
---@field enabled? boolean Opts-in for graceful shutdown.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingInstanceTerminationActionEnum "DELETE"|"INSTANCE_TERMINATION_ACTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"STOP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SchedulingMaintenanceIntervalEnum "AS_NEEDED"|"PERIODIC"|"RECURRENT"

