---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRecaptchaOptionsConfig
---@field redirectSiteKey? string An optional field to supply a reCAPTCHA site key to be used for all the rules using the redirect action with the type of GOOGLE_RECAPTCHA under the security policy. The specified site key needs to be created from the reCAPTCHA API. The user is responsible for the validity of the specified site key. If not specified, a Google-managed site key is used. This field is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR.

---Represents a rule that describes one or more match conditions along with
---the action to be taken when traffic matches this condition (allow or deny).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRule
---@field rateLimitOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptions Must be specified if the action is "rate_based_ban" or "throttle" or "fairshare". Cannot be specified for any other actions.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#securityPolicyRule for security policy rules
---@field match? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcher A match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against. If it evaluates to true, the corresponding 'action' is enforced.
---@field targetServiceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of service accounts indicating the sets of instances that are applied with this rule.
---@field direction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleDirectionEnum|string The direction in which this rule applies. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field preconfiguredWafConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfig Preconfigured WAF configuration to be applied for the rule. If the rule does not evaluate preconfigured WAF rules, i.e., if evaluatePreconfiguredWaf() is not used, this field will have no effect.
---@field networkMatch? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcher A match condition that incoming packets are evaluated against for CLOUD_ARMOR_NETWORK security policies. If it matches, the corresponding 'action' is enforced. The match criteria for a rule consists of built-in match fields (like 'srcIpRanges') and potentially multiple user-defined match fields ('userDefinedFields'). Field values may be extracted directly from the packet or derived from it (e.g. 'srcRegionCodes'). Some fields may not be present in every packet (e.g. 'srcPorts'). A user-defined field is only present if the base header is found in the packet and the entire field is in bounds. Each match field may specify which values can match it, listing one or more ranges, prefixes, or exact values that are considered a match for the field. A field value must be present in order to match a specified match field. If no match values are specified for a match field, then any field value is considered to match it, and it's not required to be present. For strings specifying '*' is also equivalent to match all. For a packet to match a rule, all specified match fields must match the corresponding field values derived from the packet. Example: networkMatch: srcIpRanges: - "192.0.2.0/24" - "198.51.100.0/24" userDefinedFields: - name: "ipv4_fragment_offset" values: - "1-0x1fff" The above match condition matches packets with a source IP in 192.0.2.0/24 or 198.51.100.0/24 and a user-defined field named "ipv4_fragment_offset" with a value between 1 and 0x1fff inclusive.
---@field priority? number An integer indicating the priority of a rule in the list. The priority must be a positive value between 0 and 2147483647. Rules are evaluated from highest to lowest priority where 0 is the highest priority and 2147483647 is the lowest priority.
---@field ruleTupleCount? number Output only. [Output Only] Calculation of the complexity of a single firewall security policy rule.
---@field redirectOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRedirectOptions Parameters defining the redirect action. Cannot be specified for any other actions. This field is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR.
---@field headerAction? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderAction Optional, additional actions that are performed on headers. This field is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR.
---@field action? string The Action to perform when the rule is matched. The following are the valid actions: - allow: allow access to target. - deny(STATUS): deny access to target, returns the HTTP response code specified. Valid values for `STATUS` are 403, 404, and 502. - rate_based_ban: limit client traffic to the configured threshold and ban the client if the traffic exceeds the threshold. Configure parameters for this action in RateLimitOptions. Requires rate_limit_options to be set. - redirect: redirect to a different target. This can either be an internal reCAPTCHA redirect, or an external URL-based redirect via a 302 response. Parameters for this action can be configured via redirectOptions. This action is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR. - throttle: limit client traffic to the configured threshold. Configure parameters for this action in rateLimitOptions. Requires rate_limit_options to be set for this. - fairshare (preview only): when traffic reaches the threshold limit, requests from the clients matching this rule begin to be rate-limited using the Fair Share algorithm. This action is only allowed in security policies of type `CLOUD_ARMOR_INTERNAL_SERVICE`.
---@field ruleNumber? string Identifier for the rule. This is only unique within the given security policy. This can only be set during rule creation, if rule number is not specified it will be generated by the server.
---@field targetResources? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of network resource URLs to which this rule applies. This field allows you to control which network's VMs get this rule. If this field is left blank, all VMs within the organization will receive the rule. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field enableLogging? boolean Denotes whether to enable logging for a particular rule. If logging is enabled, logs will be exported to the configured export destination in Stackdriver. Logs may be exported to BigQuery or Pub/Sub. Note: you cannot enable logging on "goto_next" rules. This field may only be specified when the versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field preview? boolean If set to true, the specified action is not enforced.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleDirectionEnum "EGRESS"|"INGRESS"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderAction
---@field requestHeadersToAdds? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderActionHttpHeaderOptionList The list of request headers to add or overwrite if they're already present.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderActionHttpHeaderOption
---@field headerName? string The name of the header to set.
---@field headerValue? string The value to set the named header to.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderActionHttpHeaderOptionList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleHttpHeaderActionHttpHeaderOption[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRule[]

---Represents a match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against.
---Exactly one field must be specified.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcher
---@field versionedExpr? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherVersionedExprEnum|string Preconfigured versioned expression. If this field is specified, config must also be specified. Available preconfigured expressions along with their requirements are: SRC_IPS_V1 - must specify the corresponding src_ip_range field in config.
---@field expr? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Expr User defined CEVAL expression. A CEVAL expression is used to specify match criteria such as origin.ip, source.region_code and contents in the request header. Expressions containing `evaluateThreatIntelligence` require a Cloud Armor Enterprise subscription and are not supported in Edge Policies nor in Regional Policies. Expressions containing `evaluatePreconfiguredExpr('sourceiplist-*')` require a Cloud Armor Enterprise subscription and are only supported in Global Security Policies.
---@field config? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfig The configuration options available when specifying versioned_expr. This field must be specified if versioned_expr is specified and cannot be specified if versioned_expr is not specified.
---@field exprOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptions The configuration options available when specifying a user defined CEVAL expression (i.e., 'expr').

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfig
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of src_ip_ranges allowed is 10.
---@field destIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList CIDR IP address range. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field layer4Configs? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4ConfigList Pairs of IP protocols and ports that the rule should match. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4Config
---@field ports? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList An optional list of ports to which this rule applies. This field is only applicable for UDP or TCP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. If not specified, this rule applies to connections through any port. Example inputs include: ["22"],["80","443"], and ["12345-12349"]. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field ipProtocol? string The IP protocol to which this rule applies. The protocol type is required when creating a firewall rule. This value can either be one of the following well known protocol strings (tcp,udp, icmp, esp,ah, ipip, sctp), or the IP protocol number.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4ConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4Config[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptions
---@field recaptchaOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptionsRecaptchaOptions reCAPTCHA configuration options to be applied for the rule. If the rule does not evaluate reCAPTCHA tokens, this field has no effect.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptionsRecaptchaOptions
---@field actionTokenSiteKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of site keys to be used during the validation of reCAPTCHA action-tokens. The provided site keys need to be created from reCAPTCHA API under the same project where the security policy is created.
---@field sessionTokenSiteKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of site keys to be used during the validation of reCAPTCHA session-tokens. The provided site keys need to be created from reCAPTCHA API under the same project where the security policy is created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherVersionedExprEnum "FIREWALL"|"SRC_IPS_V1"

---Represents a match condition that incoming network traffic is evaluated
---against.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcher
---@field srcRegionCodes? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Two-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code associated with the source IP address.
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Source IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDR prefixes, in standard text format.
---@field userDefinedFields? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcherUserDefinedFieldMatchList User-defined fields. Each element names a defined field and lists the matching values for that field.
---@field srcPorts? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Source port numbers for TCP/UDP/SCTP. Each element can be a 16-bit unsigned decimal number (e.g. "80") or range (e.g. "0-1023").
---@field destPorts? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Destination port numbers for TCP/UDP/SCTP. Each element can be a 16-bit unsigned decimal number (e.g. "80") or range (e.g. "0-1023").
---@field srcAsns? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.IntegerList BGP Autonomous System Number associated with the source IP address.
---@field destIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Destination IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDR prefixes, in standard text format.
---@field ipProtocols? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList IPv4 protocol / IPv6 next header (after extension headers). Each element can be an 8-bit unsigned decimal number (e.g. "6"), range (e.g. "253-254"), or one of the following protocol names: "tcp", "udp", "icmp", "esp", "ah", "ipip", or "sctp".

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcherUserDefinedFieldMatch
---@field name? string Name of the user-defined field, as given in the definition.
---@field values? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Matching values of the field. Each element can be a 32-bit unsigned decimal or hexadecimal (starting with "0x") number (e.g. "64") or range (e.g. "0x400-0x7ff").

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcherUserDefinedFieldMatchList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcherUserDefinedFieldMatch[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfig
---@field exclusions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionList A list of exclusions to apply during preconfigured WAF evaluation.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusion
---@field targetRuleIds? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList A list of target rule IDs under the WAF rule set to apply the preconfigured WAF exclusion. If omitted, it refers to all the rule IDs under the WAF rule set.
---@field targetRuleSet? string Target WAF rule set to apply the preconfigured WAF exclusion.
---@field requestQueryParamsToExclude? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList A list of request query parameter names whose value will be excluded from inspection during preconfigured WAF evaluation. Note that the parameter can be in the query string or in the POST body.
---@field requestUrisToExclude? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList A list of request URIs from the request line to be excluded from inspection during preconfigured WAF evaluation. When specifying this field, the query or fragment part should be excluded.
---@field requestCookiesToExclude? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList A list of request cookie names whose value will be excluded from inspection during preconfigured WAF evaluation.
---@field requestHeadersToExclude? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList A list of request header names whose value will be excluded from inspection during preconfigured WAF evaluation.
---@field requestBodiesToExclude? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList A list of request body fields to be excluded from inspection during preconfigured WAF evaluation.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParams
---@field op? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsOpEnum|string The match operator for the field.
---@field val? string The value of the field.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParams[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionFieldParamsOpEnum "CONTAINS"|"ENDS_WITH"|"EQUALS"|"EQUALS_ANY"|"STARTS_WITH"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusionList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRulePreconfiguredWafConfigExclusion[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptions
---@field exceedAction? string Action to take for requests that are above the configured rate limit threshold, to either deny with a specified HTTP response code, or redirect to a different endpoint. Valid options are `deny(STATUS)`, where valid values for `STATUS` are 403, 404, 429, and 502, and `redirect`, where the redirect parameters come from `exceedRedirectOptions` below. The `redirect` action is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR.
---@field enforceOnKey? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyEnum|string Determines the key to enforce the rate_limit_threshold on. Possible values are: - ALL: A single rate limit threshold is applied to all the requests matching this rule. This is the default value if "enforceOnKey" is not configured. - IP: The source IP address of the request is the key. Each IP has this limit enforced separately. - HTTP_HEADER: The value of the HTTP header whose name is configured under "enforceOnKeyName". The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes of the header value. If no such header is present in the request, the key type defaults toALL. - XFF_IP: The first IP address (i.e. the originating client IP address) specified in the list of IPs under X-Forwarded-For HTTP header. If no such header is present or the value is not a valid IP, the key defaults to the source IP address of the request i.e. key type IP. - HTTP_COOKIE: The value of the HTTP cookie whose name is configured under "enforceOnKeyName". The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes of the cookie value. If no such cookie is present in the request, the key type defaults toALL. - HTTP_PATH: The URL path of the HTTP request. The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes. - SNI: Server name indication in the TLS session of the HTTPS request. The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes. The key type defaults to ALL on a HTTP session. - REGION_CODE: The country/region from which the request originates. - TLS_JA3_FINGERPRINT: JA3 TLS/SSL fingerprint if the client connects using HTTPS, HTTP/2 or HTTP/3. If not available, the key type defaults to ALL. - USER_IP: The IP address of the originating client, which is resolved based on "userIpRequestHeaders" configured with the security policy. If there is no "userIpRequestHeaders" configuration or an IP address cannot be resolved from it, the key type defaults toIP. - ASN: The autonomous system number of the originating client. If not available, the key type defaults toALL. - TLS_JA4_FINGERPRINT: JA4 TLS/SSL fingerprint if the client connects using HTTPS, HTTP/2 or HTTP/3. If not available, the key type defaults to ALL. For "fairshare" action, this value is limited to ALL i.e. a single rate limit threshold is enforced for all the requests matching the rule.
---@field banThreshold? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsThreshold Can only be specified if the action for the rule is "rate_based_ban". If specified, the key will be banned for the configured 'ban_duration_sec' when the number of requests that exceed the 'rate_limit_threshold' also exceed this 'ban_threshold'.
---@field conformAction? string Action to take for requests that are under the configured rate limit threshold. Valid option is "allow" only.
---@field rateLimitThreshold? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsThreshold Threshold at which to begin ratelimiting.
---@field banDurationSec? number Can only be specified if the action for the rule is "rate_based_ban". If specified, determines the time (in seconds) the traffic will continue to be banned by the rate limit after the rate falls below the threshold.
---@field exceedRedirectOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRedirectOptions Parameters defining the redirect action that is used as the exceed action. Cannot be specified if the exceed action is not redirect. This field is only supported in Global Security Policies of type CLOUD_ARMOR.
---@field enforceOnKeyName? string Rate limit key name applicable only for the following key types: HTTP_HEADER -- Name of the HTTP header whose value is taken as the key value. HTTP_COOKIE -- Name of the HTTP cookie whose value is taken as the key value.
---@field enforceOnKeyConfigs? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfigList If specified, any combination of values of enforce_on_key_type/enforce_on_key_name is treated as the key on which ratelimit threshold/action is enforced. You can specify up to 3 enforce_on_key_configs. If enforce_on_key_configs is specified, enforce_on_key must not be specified.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfig
---@field enforceOnKeyType? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfigEnforceOnKeyTypeEnum|string Determines the key to enforce the rate_limit_threshold on. Possible values are: - ALL: A single rate limit threshold is applied to all the requests matching this rule. This is the default value if "enforceOnKeyConfigs" is not configured. - IP: The source IP address of the request is the key. Each IP has this limit enforced separately. - HTTP_HEADER: The value of the HTTP header whose name is configured under "enforceOnKeyName". The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes of the header value. If no such header is present in the request, the key type defaults toALL. - XFF_IP: The first IP address (i.e. the originating client IP address) specified in the list of IPs under X-Forwarded-For HTTP header. If no such header is present or the value is not a valid IP, the key defaults to the source IP address of the request i.e. key type IP. - HTTP_COOKIE: The value of the HTTP cookie whose name is configured under "enforceOnKeyName". The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes of the cookie value. If no such cookie is present in the request, the key type defaults toALL. - HTTP_PATH: The URL path of the HTTP request. The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes. - SNI: Server name indication in the TLS session of the HTTPS request. The key value is truncated to the first 128 bytes. The key type defaults to ALL on a HTTP session. - REGION_CODE: The country/region from which the request originates. - TLS_JA3_FINGERPRINT: JA3 TLS/SSL fingerprint if the client connects using HTTPS, HTTP/2 or HTTP/3. If not available, the key type defaults to ALL. - USER_IP: The IP address of the originating client, which is resolved based on "userIpRequestHeaders" configured with the security policy. If there is no "userIpRequestHeaders" configuration or an IP address cannot be resolved from it, the key type defaults toIP. - ASN: The autonomous system number of the originating client. If not available, the key type defaults toALL. - TLS_JA4_FINGERPRINT: JA4 TLS/SSL fingerprint if the client connects using HTTPS, HTTP/2 or HTTP/3. If not available, the key type defaults to ALL.
---@field enforceOnKeyName? string Rate limit key name applicable only for the following key types: HTTP_HEADER -- Name of the HTTP header whose value is taken as the key value. HTTP_COOKIE -- Name of the HTTP cookie whose value is taken as the key value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfigEnforceOnKeyTypeEnum "ALL"|"ALL_IPS"|"ASN"|"HTTP_COOKIE"|"HTTP_HEADER"|"HTTP_PATH"|"IP"|"REGION_CODE"|"SNI"|"TLS_JA3_FINGERPRINT"|"TLS_JA4_FINGERPRINT"|"USER_IP"|"XFF_IP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyConfig[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsEnforceOnKeyEnum "ALL"|"ALL_IPS"|"ASN"|"HTTP_COOKIE"|"HTTP_HEADER"|"HTTP_PATH"|"IP"|"REGION_CODE"|"SNI"|"TLS_JA3_FINGERPRINT"|"TLS_JA4_FINGERPRINT"|"USER_IP"|"XFF_IP"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRateLimitOptionsThreshold
---@field intervalSec? number Interval over which the threshold is computed.
---@field count? number Number of HTTP(S) requests for calculating the threshold.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRedirectOptions
---@field target? string Target for the redirect action. This is required if the type is EXTERNAL_302 and cannot be specified for GOOGLE_RECAPTCHA.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRedirectOptionsTypeEnum|string Type of the redirect action. Possible values are: - GOOGLE_RECAPTCHA: redirect to reCAPTCHA for manual challenge assessment. - EXTERNAL_302: redirect to a different URL via a 302 response.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyRuleRedirectOptionsTypeEnum "EXTERNAL_302"|"GOOGLE_RECAPTCHA"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyTypeEnum "CLOUD_ARMOR"|"CLOUD_ARMOR_EDGE"|"CLOUD_ARMOR_INTERNAL_SERVICE"|"CLOUD_ARMOR_NETWORK"|"FIREWALL"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyUserDefinedField
---@field name? string The name of this field. Must be unique within the policy.
---@field base? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyUserDefinedFieldBaseEnum|string The base relative to which 'offset' is measured. Possible values are: - IPV4: Points to the beginning of the IPv4 header. - IPV6: Points to the beginning of the IPv6 header. - TCP: Points to the beginning of the TCP header, skipping over any IPv4 options or IPv6 extension headers. Not present for non-first fragments. - UDP: Points to the beginning of the UDP header, skipping over any IPv4 options or IPv6 extension headers. Not present for non-first fragments. required
---@field offset? number Offset of the first byte of the field (in network byte order) relative to 'base'.
---@field size? number Size of the field in bytes. Valid values: 1-4.
---@field mask? string If specified, apply this mask (bitwise AND) to the field to ignore bits before matching. Encoded as a hexadecimal number (starting with "0x"). The last byte of the field (in network byte order) corresponds to the least significant byte of the mask.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyUserDefinedFieldBaseEnum "IPV4"|"IPV6"|"TCP"|"UDP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyUserDefinedFieldList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecurityPolicyUserDefinedField[]

---The authentication and authorization settings for a BackendService.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SecuritySettings
---@field subjectAltNames? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Optional. A list of Subject Alternative Names (SANs) that the client verifies during a mutual TLS handshake with an server/endpoint for thisBackendService. When the server presents its X.509 certificate to the client, the client inspects the certificate'ssubjectAltName field. If the field contains one of the specified values, the communication continues. Otherwise, it fails. This additional check enables the client to verify that the server is authorized to run the requested service. Note that the contents of the server certificate's subjectAltName field are configured by the Public Key Infrastructure which provisions server identities. Only applies to a global BackendService withloadBalancingScheme set to INTERNAL_SELF_MANAGED. Only applies when BackendService has an attachedclientTlsPolicy with clientCertificate (mTLS mode).
---@field authentication? string [Deprecated] Use clientTlsPolicy instead.
---@field awsV4Authentication? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AWSV4Signature The configuration needed to generate a signature for access to private storage buckets that support AWS's Signature Version 4 for authentication. Allowed only for INTERNET_IP_PORT and INTERNET_FQDN_PORT NEG backends.
---@field clientTlsPolicy? string Optional. A URL referring to a networksecurity.ClientTlsPolicy resource that describes how clients should authenticate with this service's backends. clientTlsPolicy only applies to a globalBackendService with the loadBalancingScheme set to INTERNAL_SELF_MANAGED. If left blank, communications are not encrypted.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.SendDiagnosticInterruptInstancesRequest
---@field zone string The name of the zone for this request.
