---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.UpdateAccessConfigInstancesRequest
---@field securityPolicy? string The resource URL for the security policy associated with this access config.
---@field natIP? string Applies to accessConfigs (IPv4) only. Anexternal IP address associated with this instance. Specify an unused static external IP address available to the project or leave this field undefined to use an IP from a shared ephemeral IP address pool. If you specify a static external IP address, it must live in the same region as the zone of the instance.
---@field publicPtrDomainName? string The DNS domain name for the public PTR record. You can set this field only if the `setPublicPtr` field is enabled inaccessConfig. If this field is unspecified inipv6AccessConfig, a default PTR record will be created for first IP in associated external IPv6 range.
---@field name? string The name of this access configuration. In accessConfigs (IPv4), the default and recommended name is External NAT, but you can use any arbitrary string, such as My external IP orNetwork Access. In ipv6AccessConfigs, the recommend name is External IPv6.
---@field networkTier? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AccessConfigNetworkTierEnum|string This signifies the networking tier used for configuring this access configuration and can only take the following values: PREMIUM,STANDARD. If an AccessConfig is specified without a valid external IP address, an ephemeral IP will be created with this networkTier. If an AccessConfig with a valid external IP address is specified, it must match that of the networkTier associated with the Address resource owning that IP.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#accessConfig for access configs.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AccessConfigTypeEnum|string The type of configuration. In accessConfigs (IPv4), the default and only option is ONE_TO_ONE_NAT. Inipv6AccessConfigs, the default and only option isDIRECT_IPV6.
---@field externalIpv6? string Applies to ipv6AccessConfigs only. The first IPv6 address of the external IPv6 range associated with this instance, prefix length is stored inexternalIpv6PrefixLength in ipv6AccessConfig. To use a static external IP address, it must be unused and in the same region as the instance's zone. If not specified, Google Cloud will automatically assign an external IPv6 address from the instance's subnetwork.
---@field setPublicPtr? boolean Specifies whether a public DNS 'PTR' record should be created to map the external IP address of the instance to a DNS domain name. This field is not used in ipv6AccessConfig. A default PTR record will be created if the VM has external IPv6 range associated.
---@field externalIpv6PrefixLength? number Applies to ipv6AccessConfigs only. The prefix length of the external IPv6 range.
---@field networkInterface string The name of the network interface where the access config is attached.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field zone string The name of the zone for this request.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field instance string The instance name for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.UpdateAutoscalersRequest
---@field autoscalingPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AutoscalingPolicy The configuration parameters for the autoscaling algorithm. You can define one or more signals for an autoscaler: cpuUtilization,customMetricUtilizations, andloadBalancingUtilization. If none of these are specified, the default will be to autoscale based oncpuUtilization to 0.6 or 60%.
---@field target? string URL of the managed instance group that this autoscaler will scale. This field is required when creating an autoscaler.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field selfLink? string [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field recommendedSize? number Output only. [Output Only] Target recommended MIG size (number of instances) computed by autoscaler. Autoscaler calculates the recommended MIG size even when the autoscaling policy mode is different from ON. This field is empty when autoscaler is not connected to an existing managed instance group or autoscaler did not generate its prediction.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field region? string Output only. [Output Only] URL of theregion where the instance group resides (for autoscalers living in regional scope).
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#autoscaler for autoscalers.
---@field scalingScheduleStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ScalingScheduleStatusMap Output only. [Output Only] Status information of existing scaling schedules.
---@field statusDetails? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AutoscalerStatusDetailsList [Output Only] Human-readable details about the current state of the autoscaler. Read the documentation forCommonly returned status messages for examples of status messages you might encounter.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AutoscalerStatusEnum|string [Output Only] The status of the autoscaler configuration. Current set of possible values: - PENDING: Autoscaler backend hasn't read new/updated configuration. - DELETING: Configuration is being deleted. - ACTIVE: Configuration is acknowledged to be effective. Some warnings might be present in the statusDetails field. - ERROR: Configuration has errors. Actionable for users. Details are present in the statusDetails field. New values might be added in the future.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field autoscaler? string Name of the autoscaler to update.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field zone string Name of the zone for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.UpdateBackendBucketsRequest
---@field customResponseHeaders? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringList Headers that the Application Load Balancer should add to proxied responses.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field loadBalancingScheme? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketLoadBalancingSchemeEnum|string The value can only be INTERNAL_MANAGED for cross-region internal layer 7 load balancer. If loadBalancingScheme is not specified, the backend bucket can be used by classic global external load balancers, or global application external load balancers, or both.
---@field selfLink? string [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field cdnPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketCdnPolicy Cloud CDN configuration for this BackendBucket.
---@field kind? string Output only. Type of the resource.
---@field description? string An optional textual description of the resource; provided by the client when the resource is created.
---@field id? string [Output Only] Unique identifier for the resource; defined by the server.
---@field creationTimestamp? string [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field enableCdn? boolean If true, enable Cloud CDN for this BackendBucket.
---@field region? string Output only. [Output Only] URL of the region where the regional backend bucket resides. This field is not applicable to global backend buckets. You must specify this field as part of the HTTP request URL. It is not settable as a field in the request body.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketParams Input only. [Input Only] Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field usedBy? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketUsedByList Output only. [Output Only] List of resources referencing that backend bucket.
---@field edgeSecurityPolicy? string [Output Only] The resource URL for the edge security policy associated with this backend bucket.
---@field bucketName? string Cloud Storage bucket name.
---@field compressionMode? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.BackendBucketCompressionModeEnum|string Compress text responses using Brotli or gzip compression, based on the client's Accept-Encoding header.
