---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.UpdateInstancesRequest
---@field hostname? string Specifies the hostname of the instance. The specified hostname must be RFC1035 compliant. If hostname is not specified, the default hostname is [INSTANCE_NAME].c.[PROJECT_ID].internal when using the global DNS, and [INSTANCE_NAME].[ZONE].c.[PROJECT_ID].internal when using zonal DNS.
---@field guestAccelerators? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AcceleratorConfigList A list of the type and count of accelerator cards attached to the instance.
---@field displayDevice? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.DisplayDevice Enables display device for the instance.
---@field sourceMachineImage? string Source machine image
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Tags Tags to apply to this instance. Tags are used to identify valid sources or targets for network firewalls and are specified by the client during instance creation. The tags can be later modified by the setTags method. Each tag within the list must comply withRFC1035. Multiple tags can be specified via the 'tags.items' field.
---@field fingerprint? string Specifies a fingerprint for this resource, which is essentially a hash of the instance's contents and used for optimistic locking. The fingerprint is initially generated by Compute Engine and changes after every request to modify or update the instance. You must always provide an up-to-date fingerprint hash in order to update the instance. To see the latest fingerprint, make get() request to the instance.
---@field instanceEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.CustomerEncryptionKey Encrypts suspended data for an instance with acustomer-managed encryption key. If you are creating a new instance, this field will encrypt the local SSD and in-memory contents of the instance during the suspend operation. If you do not provide an encryption key when creating the instance, then the local SSD and in-memory contents will be encrypted using an automatically generated key during the suspend operation.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.AttachedDiskList Array of disks associated with this instance. Persistent disks must be created before you can assign them.
---@field partnerMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StructuredEntriesMap Partner Metadata assigned to the instance. A map from a subdomain (namespace) to entries map.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field privateIpv6GoogleAccess? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstancePrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum|string The private IPv6 google access type for the VM. If not specified, use INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK as default.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.InstanceStatusEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The status of the instance. One of the following values: PROVISIONING, STAGING,RUNNING, STOPPING, SUSPENDING,SUSPENDED, REPAIRING, andTERMINATED. For more information about the status of the instance, see Instance life cycle.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field eraseWindowsVssSignature? boolean Specifies whether the disks restored from source snapshots or source machine image should erase Windows specific VSS signature.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.StringMap Labels to apply to this instance. These can be later modified by the setLabels method.
---@field networkPerformanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.NetworkPerformanceConfig
---@field sourceMachineImageEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.CustomerEncryptionKey Source machine image encryption key when creating an instance from a machine image.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.ShieldedVmConfig Output only. Deprecating, please use shielded_instance_config.
