---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WireList gcp.unstable.compute_beta.Wire[]

---The properties of a wire.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WireProperties
---@field bandwidthAllocation? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WirePropertiesBandwidthAllocationEnum|string The configuration of the bandwidth allocation, one of the following: - ALLOCATE_PER_WIRE: configures a separate unmetered bandwidth allocation (and associated charges) for each wire in the group. - SHARED_WITH_WIRE_GROUP: this is the default behavior, which configures one unmetered bandwidth allocation for the wire group. The unmetered bandwidth is divided equally across each wire in the group, but dynamic throttling reallocates unused unmetered bandwidth from unused or underused wires to other wires in the group.
---@field faultResponse? gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WirePropertiesFaultResponseEnum|string Response when a fault is detected in a pseudowire: - NONE: default. - DISABLE_PORT: set the port line protocol down when inline probes detect a fault. This setting is only permitted on port mode pseudowires.
---@field bandwidthUnmetered? string The unmetered bandwidth in Gigabits per second, using decimal units. `10` is 10 Gbps, `100` is 100 Gbps. The bandwidth must be greater than 0.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WirePropertiesBandwidthAllocationEnum "ALLOCATE_PER_WIRE"|"SHARED_WITH_WIRE_GROUP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WirePropertiesFaultResponseEnum "DISABLE_PORT"|"NONE"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WithdrawPublicAdvertisedPrefixesRequest
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field publicAdvertisedPrefix string The name of the public advertised prefix. It should comply with RFC1035.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_beta.WithdrawPublicDelegatedPrefixesRequest
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field region string The name of theregion where the public delegated prefix is located. It should comply with RFC1035.
---@field publicDelegatedPrefix string The name of the public delegated prefix. It should comply with RFC1035.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

